/* 心斋 · 陌生人的陪伴（compassion）+ 佛学开示（dharma）
   规范见《心斋段_口吻卡.md》v2：陪伴段先接住人，开示段先把故事讲完，话自己长出来。
   dharma 里的 \n 用于分段，页面按 pre-line 渲染。 */
var ASK_CARE = {

'自卑、不自信、自我否定':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。你把自己数落得这么熟练，恐怕已经数落很多年了。你不是没有价值，是把自己的好，看得太轻了。今天只做一件事：像对朋友那样，跟自己说一句话。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. You have gotten very good at listing your faults — probably for years now. It is not that you have no worth; it is that you keep weighing it too lightly. One thing today: say something to yourself the way you would to a friend.',
  dharma:'佛经里有个故事。\n一个人穷了一辈子，四处讨饭，直到有人指给他看：你衣服的夹层里，缝着一颗宝珠。\n他从来没丢过，他只是不知道。\n你身上也有这东西——不是本事，不是成绩，是你本来就有的那份分量。\n今晚写下一件你做过的好事，很小的一件也行。你会发现，用来数落自己的那份清单，并不全是真的。',
  dharmaEn:'There is a story in the scriptures.\nA man was poor his whole life, begging from place to place — until someone pointed at him and said: there is a jewel sewn into the lining of your coat.\nHe had never lost it. He simply did not know it was there.\nYou carry the same kind of thing — not talent, not achievement, but the worth you were born with.\nTonight, write down one good thing you have done, even a small one. You may find that the list you use against yourself is not entirely true.'
},

'累、被掏空、职业倦怠':{
  compassion:'hi 朋友，先坐下。累成这样，不是一天两天了。你不用急着证明自己还行——先问自己一句：这肩上，是不是背得太满了？',
  compassionEn:'Hi friend, sit down first. To be this tired, it did not start today. You do not have to prove you are fine — ask yourself one thing first: is the load on your shoulders simply too heavy?',
  dharma:'佛经里有个弹琴的故事。\n有位比丘修行很拼命，日夜不歇，身体眼看要垮。佛陀没责备他，只问了一句：你从前在家，弹过琴吧？\n他说弹过。佛陀说：弦绷得太紧，一弹就断；放得太松，又发不出声。\n他听懂了，把力气收回来一点，后来反而走得远。\n你现在的弦，比他还紧。今晚先松一格——少做一件事，天不会塌。',
  dharmaEn:'There is a story about playing the lute.\nA monk practiced so hard, day and night without rest, that his body was about to break. The Buddha did not scold him. He only asked: you used to play the lute at home, didn’t you?\nHe said yes. The Buddha said: wound too tight, the string snaps; left too loose, it makes no sound.\nHe understood, pulled his effort back a notch, and walked further that way.\nYour string is tighter than his right now. Loosen it one notch tonight — do one thing less. The sky will not fall.'
},

'心乱、静不下来、杂念纷飞':{
  compassion:'来，先坐下。心乱不是你有毛病，是它太久没被安静地看过了。别急着把念头按下去，按得越用力，它跳得越凶。先把呼吸放慢一点，比平时长一点就够。',
  compassionEn:'Come, sit down first. A restless mind does not mean something is wrong with you; it means your mind has not been watched quietly in a long time. Do not force the thoughts down — the harder you press, the higher they jump. Just make one breath a little longer than usual.',
  dharma:'我在院里搁过一盆浑水。\n刚搅起来的时候，什么都看不见。有位老修行叫我别动它，放着。\n半个时辰过去，泥沙自己沉下去了，水清了。\n你的心现在就是这样一盆水。念头不用赶，坐一会儿，它自己会沉。\n今晚睡前给自己五分钟，什么都不做，只看着念头来，看着念头走。',
  dharmaEn:'I once left a basin of muddy water in the yard.\nJust stirred up, you could see nothing in it. An old practitioner told me to leave it alone.\nHalf an hour later the silt had settled by itself, and the water was clear.\nYour mind is that basin right now. The thoughts need no chasing. Sit a while, and they will settle on their own.\nTonight before sleep, give yourself five minutes. Do nothing. Watch the thoughts come, and watch them go.'
},

'患得患失、害怕失去':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。怕失去的时候，人会把手攥得很紧——可攥得太紧的东西，自己先疼。先别急着看住谁。你今天能做的，只是把自己过稳一点。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. When we fear losing someone, the hand grips tight — and what we grip too hard hurts us first. Do not rush to hold on to anyone. What you can do today is simply steady yourself.',
  dharma:'佛陀讲过一把沙。\n手掌摊开，沙就留在手里；手指一攥，沙从缝里全漏了。\n有人问：那我该怎么拿住它？\n佛陀说：摊开。\n你怕失去的那个人、那段关系，也是这样。抓得越紧漏得越快，把手放松一点，它反而留得住。',
  dharmaEn:'The Buddha once spoke of a handful of sand.\nKeep the palm open and the sand stays; close your fingers and it all runs through.\nSomeone asked: then how should I hold it?\nThe Buddha said: keep the hand open.\nThe person, the relationship you are afraid of losing — it works the same way. Grip tighter, lose faster. Loosen your hand, and it may stay.'
},

'空虚、人生没意义':{
  compassion:'来，先坐。心里空的时候，别急着找一个大答案来填。意义不是想出来的，是活出来的。今天找一件小事认真做完，为别人，或为自己都行。',
  compassionEn:'Come, sit first. When you feel empty, do not rush to fill it with a grand answer. Meaning is not thought up; it is lived out. Find one small thing to do well today — for someone else, or for yourself.',
  dharma:'佛经里有个比喻，叫"毒箭"。\n有人中了一箭，疼得厉害，却不肯拔——先要弄明白：这箭是谁射的？什么木头做的？用什么羽毛？\n问题还没问完，人就死了。\n佛陀讲这个，是提醒弟子：有些问题追问一辈子也没有答案，而生活就在眼前。\n你问"活着有什么意义"，这问题可以先挂着。今晚先做一件小事，给谁倒杯水也行，明天再问它。',
  dharmaEn:'The scriptures have an image called "the poisoned arrow".\nA man was hit by an arrow and was in great pain, yet he refused to have it pulled out. First he wanted to know: who shot it? What wood was the shaft? What feathers?\nBefore the questions were finished, the man was dead.\nThe Buddha told this to remind his students: some questions can be asked for a lifetime without an answer, while life is right in front of you.\nYour question — what is the meaning of life — can hang there for now. Do one small thing tonight. Pour someone a cup of water. Ask the question again tomorrow.'
},

'讨好型、不会拒绝、关系累':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。什么都答应下来的人，最后往往最累，也最委屈——因为你把所有人都照顾到了，除了你自己。这周挑一件小事，诚实地拒绝一次，看看天会不会塌。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. The person who agrees to everything ends up the most tired and the most resentful — because everyone is cared for except you. Pick one small thing this week and honestly decline it. See whether the sky falls.',
  dharma:'有个修慈悲的年轻人，修了几年，越修越累。\n他去找上师，上师只问了一句：你那份慈悲的名单，第一个写的是谁？\n他答不上来。\n上师说：名单上第一个，应当是你自己。你不在里面，这份慈悲撑不了多久。\n今晚先试着把那句拒绝说给自己听——"这件事我做不到"。说顺了，明天再对别人说。',
  dharmaEn:'A young man practiced compassion for years, and the more he practiced, the more tired he became.\nHe went to his teacher, who asked only one question: on that list of people you feel compassion for, whose name is first?\nHe could not answer.\nThe teacher said: the first name should be your own. If you are not on the list, the compassion will not hold for long.\nTonight, try saying the refusal to yourself first — "I cannot do this one." Once it comes out smoothly, say it to someone else tomorrow.'
},

'被人欺骗欺负、老实受气':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。受了气还劝自己"算了"的人，心里的账其实一直在记。善良不是任人欺负，你的好意也不该拿来自伤。先把该留的证据留下，把该说的话平静说一次。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. When you swallow an insult and tell yourself to let it go, the mind keeps its own accounts. Kindness does not mean being available for harm, and your goodness should not be used against you. Keep the records you need, and say the thing once, calmly.',
  dharma:'佛经里记过一件事。\n有人跑到佛陀面前，骂了很久。佛陀一直安静地听着。\n那人骂累了，佛陀才问：你带礼物去别人家，对方不收，礼物归谁？\n他说：当然是我带回去。\n佛陀说：你刚才那些话，我没有收。\n你不必做到不生气。但可以学着不签收——他送他的，你先放下；该留的证据留下，该找的人去找。',
  dharmaEn:'The scriptures record an incident.\nA man came before the Buddha and insulted him for a long time. The Buddha listened quietly.\nWhen the man had worn himself out, the Buddha asked: if you bring a gift to someone’s house and they do not accept it, whose gift is it?\nHe said: it goes back with me, of course.\nThe Buddha said: those words of yours — I have not accepted them.\nYou do not have to stop being angry. But you can learn not to sign for the delivery. He sends his; you set it down. Keep the records you need, and go find the people who can actually act.'
},

'刷手机停不下来、熬夜戒不掉':{
  compassion:'hi 朋友。先说一句：半夜还在刷，不是你没出息，那东西本来就是被设计成让人停不下来的。今晚别跟自己较劲，只做一件小事——把充电器挪到卧室外面。',
  compassionEn:'Hi friend. First, one thing: scrolling at midnight does not mean you are weak. That thing was designed so you cannot stop. Tonight, do not fight yourself. Do one small thing — move the charger out of the bedroom.',
  dharma:'佛经里讲过一个画面。\n沙漠里的鹿，远远看见一片水光，一路追过去。跑到跟前，什么也没有。\n它更渴了，又看见前面有水光，又追。\n佛陀用它说：有一种渴，是越追越渴的。\n你半夜盯着的那块屏幕，就是那片水光。今晚试着不看它十分钟，躺下来，让渴自己过去。',
  dharmaEn:'The scriptures describe a scene.\nA deer in the desert sees a shimmer of water far off and runs toward it. It arrives — nothing there.\nThirstier now, it sees more water ahead, and runs again.\nThe Buddha used this to say: there is a kind of thirst that grows the more you chase it.\nThat screen at midnight is the shimmer. Tonight, try not looking at it for ten minutes. Lie down and let the thirst pass on its own.'
},

'分手失恋、走不出情伤':{
  compassion:'朋友，坐一会儿。这种疼，不会因为别人说一句"会过去的"就轻一点。你不用逼自己现在就走出来——先允许自己难过，难过不是没出息。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit with me a while. This kind of pain does not get lighter just because someone says it will pass. You do not have to force yourself out of it today — let yourself be sad first. Being sad is not weakness.',
  dharma:'佛经里有个比喻，叫"筏喻"。\n有人编了只木筏过河，水很急，他靠着它到了对岸。上岸以后，他却把筏子背起来，继续往前走。\n佛陀说：筏子是渡河用的，上了岸，就不必再背着它。\n那段关系就是那只筏子。它把你送到了今天站的地方，它的用处，到这里就结束了。\n今晚把那些翻过一百遍的聊天记录收进一个文件夹，不删也行，只是不再打开。',
  dharmaEn:'The scriptures have an image called "the raft".\nA man built a raft to cross a river. The water was swift, but he made it to the other side. Once ashore, he put the raft on his back and kept walking.\nThe Buddha said: the raft is for crossing. Once you are across, you need not carry it further.\nThat relationship was your raft. It carried you to where you stand today, and there its work ends.\nTonight, move those messages you have read a hundred times into one folder. You do not have to delete them — just stop opening them.'
},

'社恐、不敢在人前说话':{
  compassion:'hi 朋友，先坐下。你不是不想说话，是太怕说错。那种"所有人都在看我"的感觉是真的，但多半不是别人给的，是你自己先站到了台中央。',
  compassionEn:'Hi friend, sit down first. It is not that you do not want to speak; you are afraid of getting it wrong. That feeling of everyone watching is real — but most of it is not from them. You put yourself on the stage first.',
  dharma:'古书里有个怕影子的人。\n他走在路上，看见自己的影子，越看越怕，就拼命往前跑。跑得越快，影子追得越紧，最后他一头栽倒，影子压在他身上。\n其实他站住，影子就停在他脚下了。\n你怕的那道目光，就是这道影子。\n今天只做一件小到不可能失败的事：买点东西，看着店员的眼睛说一句"谢谢"，说完就走，不用多讲一个字。',
  dharmaEn:'There is a man in an old story who was afraid of his own shadow.\nWalking down the road, he saw the shadow, grew frightened, and ran. The faster he ran, the closer it followed, until he fell — and the shadow lay right on top of him.\nHad he simply stood still, the shadow would have stayed under his feet.\nThe eyes you fear are that shadow.\nToday, do one thing too small to fail: buy something, look the clerk in the eye, say "thank you" — then leave. No need to say one word more.'
},

'和父母说不到一起、被催婚':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。两头都委屈：他们怕你过得不好，你怕自己活得不像自己。他们的话烫，你的耳朵也烫，别硬接。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Both sides are hurting: they are afraid you will not be well, and you are afraid of not living your own life. Their words are hot. So are your ears. Do not take it bare-handed.',
  dharma:'有位师父教过一个办法。\n他让徒弟端一杯滚烫的茶去给母亲。徒弟说烫。师父说：烫你就换手，别撒，也别硬端。\n母亲念叨你，就是那杯烫茶。你可以听，但不必每个字都端在手里。\n今晚给家里打个电话，只问一句"最近身体怎么样"，聊三句就说要去吃饭，先挂。这也算往前走了一步。',
  dharmaEn:'A teacher gave his student a way to handle this.\nHe told the student to carry a cup of scalding tea to his mother. The student said it was too hot. The teacher said: when it is hot, change hands. Do not spill it, and do not grip it bare.\nWhen your mother keeps on at you, that is the hot cup. You can listen without holding every word in your hands.\nTonight, call home and ask just one thing — how are you feeling lately. After three sentences, say you are going to eat, and hang up. That is still a step forward.'
},

'孩子不听话、青春期叛逆':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。你现在最累的不是孩子，是"必须管好他"这件事压在你身上。他越大越像另一个人，这不是你教坏了。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. What exhausts you is not the child; it is the weight of "I must keep him in line". The older he grows, the more he becomes his own person. That does not mean you raised him wrong.',
  dharma:'有个老农放过一辈子牛。\n人家问他怎么管得住一群牛。他说：我不拉它，不喂它，我只看着它，别跑到别人田里去。\n孩子那段力气，是用来长他自己的。你拉得越紧，他越要往反方向使劲。\n今晚只守一条底线——安全。其他的，先松一格。',
  dharmaEn:'An old farmer herded cattle all his life.\nSomeone asked how he kept a whole herd in hand. He said: I do not pull them, I do not feed them. I just watch to see they do not wander into someone else’s field.\nA teenager’s strength is meant for growing himself. The tighter you pull, the harder he pulls the other way.\nTonight, hold only one line — safety. Loosen everything else by one notch.'
},

'总爱跟人比、心里不平衡':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。比出来的难受最磨人，因为你永远找得到比自己强的人。你把自己的日子过成了一场考试，考官还是别人。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. The pain of comparison grinds you down, because there is always someone ahead. You have turned your life into an exam — and the examiner is everyone else.',
  dharma:'佛经里有个故事。\n一位穷女子把身上仅有的钱买了一盏小灯，供在佛前。那天夜里风大，别人的灯都灭了，她那盏一直亮着。\n她的灯不比别人的大，也不比别人亮。\n你也是。你不是要赢过谁，你只要把手上这一盏点着。\n今晚做一件只属于你自己的小事，做完就睡，不用告诉任何人。',
  dharmaEn:'There is a story in the scriptures.\nA poor woman spent the little she had on one small lamp and offered it before the Buddha. That night the wind was strong. Other lamps went out; hers stayed lit.\nHer lamp was not bigger or brighter than the rest.\nNeither are you. You are not here to outshine anyone. You only need to keep the one in your hand lit.\nTonight, do one small thing that is only yours. Then sleep. No need to tell anyone.'
},

'夫妻感情变淡、想分开':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。日子过到没话说，不是一天冷下来的。先别急着下结论说"不爱了"——冷的火塘，很多时候只是没人添柴。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. A life that has gone quiet did not cool down in a day. Do not rush to conclude that love is gone — a cold hearth often just means no one has added wood.',
  dharma:'山里有对老夫妻，一辈子睡在同一个火塘边。\n有人问老太太，这么多年是怎么过来的。她说：火不是一次就烧起来的，是一根一根添的。有一年我们谁都不添，就那样冷了两个冬天。\n后来是谁先添的柴，她没讲。反正火又起来了。\n今晚添一根最小的柴：买一样他爱吃的东西回来，或者只说一句"早点睡"。',
  dharmaEn:'In the mountains lived an old couple who slept by the same hearth all their lives.\nSomeone asked the wife how they had lasted. She said: the fire never started all at once. It was one stick at a time. One year neither of us added any, and we were cold for two winters.\nShe never said who put the first stick back. The fire came up again anyway.\nTonight, add the smallest stick: bring home something he likes, or just say "sleep early".'
},

'失业、被裁、裸辞后迷茫':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。丢的是一份工，不是你这个人的用处在哪。慌是正常的，但别在慌里做长远的决定。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. What you lost is a job, not your worth. Panicking is normal — just do not make long-term decisions inside the panic.',
  dharma:'说一个我自己的笨办法。\n我失业那阵，每天早上照样按上班的点出门，去图书馆坐半天。不投简历的时候，就翻闲书。不是装忙，是让身体先走在路上。\n三个月后，机会是从那条走熟了的老路上来的。\n明天早上，按上班的时间起床出门，去一个能坐着看书的地方坐两个小时。方向先不论，先让身体动起来。',
  dharmaEn:'Here is a clumsy method of my own.\nWhen I lost my job, I still left the house at the usual hour every morning and sat half the day in a library. When I was not sending out applications, I read whatever was at hand. It was not busywork; it was to get my body walking the road first.\nThree months later, the opening came from that same well-worn road.\nTomorrow morning, get up at your work hour and go sit somewhere you can read for two hours. Never mind the direction. Just get the body moving.'
},

'健康焦虑、老怀疑自己生病':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。身上一点动静就被放大成最坏的结果，这份累不是装的，是真耗人。你已经查过不止一次了吧？查完那点安心，通常撑不过三天。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Every small signal in the body gets magnified into the worst possible outcome. That exhaustion is real, not imagined. You have been checked more than once, haven’t you? The relief usually does not last three days.',
  dharma:'佛陀常把自己比作医生。\n他说，他能开方子，但药要病人自己喝。有位比丘把方子背得很熟，逢人就讲，自己却一口没喝。\n佛陀问他：你背了这么多药方，病好了吗？\n你现在的方子，医生已经开过了——按时睡、少熬夜、别自己上网查症状。你缺的不是更多检查，是照着喝。\n今晚十一点前躺下，手机放到客厅。就这一味。',
  dharmaEn:'The Buddha often compared himself to a doctor.\nHe said he could write the prescription, but the patient had to drink the medicine. One monk memorized the prescriptions so well he could recite them to anyone — yet never took a single dose.\nThe Buddha asked him: you have memorized so many prescriptions. Are you well?\nYour prescription has already been written — sleep on time, stay off the late nights, stop looking up symptoms online. What you lack is not more tests; it is taking the medicine.\nTonight, lie down before eleven and leave the phone in the living room. That is the whole dose.'
},

'伴侣出轨、要不要原谅':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。这种事砸下来，晃的不是感情，是你整个人。你今天不用决定原谅还是离开。先要安全和诚实：找一个人陪着，撑不住就打当地的求助热线。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. When this lands, it is not the relationship that shakes — it is you. You do not have to decide today between forgiving and leaving. Ask for safety and honesty first: let someone stay with you, and call a local help line if it is too much.',
  dharma:'我见过一个人，丈夫出了这事，她三天没吃饭。\n我劝她先吃，她说吃不下。我说：你现在是在流血，先把血止住，别的事明天再说。\n她喝了半碗粥，睡了一觉，第二天才开始想该怎么办。\n后来她怎么决定，我没问。只知道她先把自己扶住了。\n今晚你也先扶住自己：吃点东西，让一个人陪着你。决定的事，等伤口包好了再说。',
  dharmaEn:'I once knew a woman whose husband did this. She did not eat for three days.\nI told her to eat first. She said she could not. I said: you are bleeding right now — stop the bleeding first. Everything else can wait until tomorrow.\nShe drank half a bowl of porridge, slept, and only the next day began to think about what to do.\nI never asked what she decided. I only know she steadied herself first.\nTonight, steady yourself first too: eat something, keep one person near you. Leave the decision until the wound is wrapped.'
},

'孤独、没朋友':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。孤独不是"没人要"，是心里那几根线断着，没人接住。不用等一个什么都懂你的人出现——这周先给一个人发一条具体的消息，问一句：你最近好吗。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Loneliness is not proof that nobody wants you; it is a few threads that came loose, with no one holding the other end. Do not wait for someone who understands everything. This week, send one person one concrete message: how have you been.',
  dharma:'山里冬天长，僧人们各住一间小屋。\n有位师父说：别关门等天亮，把灯点着，放在窗台上。\n对面山上的人看见，也就把自己的点上。\n灯不照亮谁，只是让那边知道：这儿还有人。\n这周你做那盏灯就够：在同一家店、同一趟车上，跟同一张脸打个招呼。第三次，他们就认得你了。',
  dharmaEn:'The mountain winters are long, and the monks each keep their own small hut.\nA teacher said: do not sit behind a closed door waiting for daylight — light your lamp and set it on the windowsill.\nWhen someone across the valley sees it, they light their own.\nA lamp does not light anyone’s way. It only lets the other side know: there is still someone here.\nThis week, being that lamp is enough: greet the same face at the same shop, on the same bus. By the third time, they will know you.'
},

'脱单难、相亲内耗':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。相亲内耗，是因为你把每次见面都当成了考试，考官还坐在对面。先把问题换一下：不是"他会不会选我"，而是"我跟他待着，安不安心"。你的日子不该只剩相亲这一件事。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Dating fatigue comes from treating every meeting as an exam — with the examiner sitting across the table. Change the question: not "will they choose me", but "do I feel at ease with this person". Your life should not be only about this.',
  dharma:'有人去寺里求姻缘，求了三年。\n师父问：这三年你都在做什么？他说：等。\n师父说：你去早市看看，挑菜的人是站着等的，还是一个摊一个摊看的？\n他说：一个摊一个摊看的。师父说：人也一样。\n不是要你多相几个。是把脚步放到自己能走的速度，见一次就只是一次。',
  dharmaEn:'Someone went to a temple to pray for a partner, and prayed for three years.\nThe teacher asked: what have you been doing these three years? He said: waiting.\nThe teacher said: go to the morning market. Do the people choosing vegetables stand and wait, or do they look stall by stall?\nHe said: they look stall by stall. The teacher said: people are the same.\nThis is not about going on more dates. It is about walking at a pace you can keep, and letting one meeting be just one meeting.'
},

'缺钱、负债、经济压力焦虑':{
  compassion:'钱的事，先把数目写清楚，再谈心。乱不在数字，在心里那句"我这辈子完了"——那是念头，不是事实。还债一步一步走，心也要留条活路：今天还吃得下、睡得着，就还有翻过来的日子。',
  compassionEn:'Write the numbers down plainly first, then talk about the mind. The chaos is not in the figure but in the thought "my life is over" — that is a thought, not a fact. Repaying happens step by step, and the heart needs room to live too: if you can still eat and sleep today, there is still a day to turn it around.',
  dharma:'从前有人背一袋石头上山，越走越沉，还不肯放下——他说：这是我自己的石头。\n挑夫说：放下，路还是你的；不放下，路就不是你的了。\n你今晚只做一件事：把每一笔欠款和利息，一个数一个数写在一张纸上。\n写完就收起来，明天再想。数摊开了，人心就不那么慌。',
  dharmaEn:'Once a man carried a sack of stones up a mountain. The higher he went, the heavier it got, and still he would not put it down — he said: these are my own stones.\nA porter passing by said: put it down, and the road is still yours. Keep carrying it, and the road is not yours anymore.\nTonight, do one thing only: write every debt and every interest figure on a single sheet of paper.\nThen put the sheet away and think about it tomorrow. Once the numbers are spread out, the panic gets quieter.'
},

'产后崩溃、新手爸妈被掏空':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下，你辛苦了。产后哭、睡不着、觉得不像自己，多半是身体和睡眠在报警，不是你不够爱孩子。请告诉产科或产检医生，也请家人替你接一班——这不是麻烦别人。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first — you have been through a lot. Crying, not sleeping, feeling unlike yourself after birth is usually the body and sleep sending an alarm, not proof that you love your baby too little. Tell your doctor, and let someone take a shift — that is not being a burden.',
  dharma:'佛经里说，两个比丘同行，一个病了。\n另一个没有说教，先给他洗身、换衣、喂药，扶他睡下。佛陀看见，只说了一句：照顾病人的人，就是在照顾我。\n你现在是两个都病着：一个是你，一个是抱着孩子的那点力气。\n今晚把夜里一班交给别人。你睡那三小时，就是在照顾你们两个人。',
  dharmaEn:'The scriptures tell of two monks traveling together when one fell ill.\nThe other did not preach. He washed him, changed his clothes, gave him medicine, and helped him lie down. Seeing this, the Buddha said only: whoever cares for the sick, cares for me.\nRight now two of you are unwell: you, and the strength that holds the baby.\nTonight, hand one night shift to someone else. Those three hours of sleep are care for both of you.'
},

'产后身材走样、恢复焦虑':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。生过孩子的身体，不是走样的身体，是撑过了一件事的身体。先把吃和睡顾好，别的排后面；真要动，先问医生你能不能开始，再慢慢来。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. A body that has given birth is not a body gone wrong; it is a body that carried something enormous. Look after food and sleep first and put the rest later. And when you do want to move, ask your doctor first, then take it slowly.',
  dharma:'我见过一个种树的。\n树苗刚移栽那年，叶子蔫、树皮也裂，他天天浇水，不掰不剪。别人笑他不管，他说：它正在长根，根没长好，枝条长得再直也没用。\n第二年春天，那棵树长得最旺。\n你的身体现在正在长根。今晚先照顾吃和睡，等医生点了头，再让它动一动。',
  dharmaEn:'I once knew a man who planted trees.\nThe year a sapling was moved, its leaves drooped and its bark split. He watered it every day and did not prune or bend it. People laughed that he did nothing. He said: it is growing roots. If the roots are not set, no straight branch will help.\nThe next spring, that tree grew the strongest of all.\nYour body is growing roots right now. Tonight, look after food and sleep, and when your doctor says yes, let it move a little.'
},

'带娃方式跟婆婆/老人分歧':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。跟老人争的常常不是方法，是"这个家谁说了算"。别在每件事上都较劲：底线跟伴侣先说定，其余的，让一步不算输。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. What you are arguing about with the older generation is often not the method but who gets to decide in this house. Do not fight on every point: settle the non-negotiables with your partner first, and letting the rest go is not losing.',
  dharma:'山脚下两条河汇到一处，撞得响，把石头都掀了起来。走远些看，它们早成了一条，分不出谁是谁。\n你跟老人现在正在撞。\n先把安全的底线跟伴侣说定，剩下的小事，明天让一步试试。多数分歧，过一两年自己就看不出来了。',
  dharmaEn:'Two rivers meet at the foot of a mountain. They crash and throw up stones. Walk a little further and they are already one river — you cannot tell which is which.\nThat is what is happening between you and the older generation now.\nSettle the safety lines with your partner first, and let one small thing go tomorrow. Most of these disagreements become invisible in a year or two.'
},

'产假结束怕回职场、全职后想复出':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。回去上班是一次过渡，不是当妈的考试。把托育和头两周写细一点，允许自己头一个月精力差，能半天半天回，就别一步到位。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Going back to work is a transition, not a test of motherhood. Write the childcare and the first two weeks out in some detail, allow your energy to be low for a month, and go back in half days if you can rather than all at once.',
  dharma:'有位师父教人下山办事。\n徒弟怕办不好，站在山口不敢走。师父说：你别想着一路走到城里，先看脚下这一步，走到那块石头；到了，再看下一块。\n徒弟就这么一段一段走，天没黑就进了城。\n你明天只走这一步：把托育和第一天的时间写好。别的，等到了那块石头再说。',
  dharmaEn:'A teacher once sent his student down the mountain on an errand.\nThe student was afraid of doing it badly and stood at the pass, unable to start. The teacher said: do not try to walk all the way to town. Look at this step, up to that stone. When you reach it, look at the next one.\nHe walked that way, one stretch at a time, and was in town before dark.\nTomorrow, walk only this step: write down the childcare and the first day. The rest waits until you reach that stone.'
},

'年龄焦虑、一事无成、怕来不及':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。年龄焦虑，多半是拿自己的时间，去比一个想象出来的时间表。别人走到哪一站，跟你没关系。今天只做一件小事，做完就是往前走。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Age anxiety usually comes from measuring your own timing against an imagined schedule. Where others have arrived has nothing to do with you. Do one small thing today, and that already counts as moving forward.',
  dharma:'我年轻时总觉得自己落后，问过一位师父。\n他指着院里的树说：你数数，它一年长几寸？我说看不出来。他说：看不出，是因为它天天在长。\n又说：树不跟旁边的树比高，它只往有光的地方去。\n你只看得见别人长出来的那一段，看不见他们土里的那几年。\n这周只做一件这个月能有结果的小事，做完就算了。',
  dharmaEn:'When I was young I always felt behind, so I asked a teacher about it.\nHe pointed at a tree in the yard and said: count how much it grows in a year. I said I could not tell. He said: you cannot tell because it grows every day.\nThen he said: a tree does not compare its height with the tree beside it. It only grows toward the light.\nYou only see the part others have grown. You do not see the years they spent underground.\nThis week, do one small thing that can show a result this month. Then let it be done.'
},

'怕变老、初老焦虑':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。看见白发和细纹就心慌，怕的不是老，是"以后就不被人看见了"。这份怕很真实。今天先把睡眠、力气和几个你喜欢的人守住——老去的样子，很大一部分由这些决定。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. What frightens you at the sight of grey hair and fine lines is not age itself — it is the fear of no longer being seen. That fear is real. Today, protect your sleep, your strength, and a few people you like; much of how we age is decided by those.',
  dharma:'我这儿有个茶碗，用了二十多年。口沿磕了个小口子，把手也磨亮了。\n有人来，我还是拿它倒茶。新碗好看，可茶倒进去，喝出来是两回事。\n东西用久了，留下的是手磨出来的那层光。\n人也一样。皱纹和手上的茧，是有人跟你相处过的证据。\n今晚照镜子时，别急着挑毛病，只对自己说一句：这些年，辛苦了。',
  dharmaEn:'I have a tea bowl here that I have used for over twenty years. There is a small chip on the rim, and the handle is worn smooth.\nWhen someone visits, I still pour from it. New bowls look better, but the tea tastes like something else.\nWhen a thing is used that long, what stays is the sheen your hand has left on it.\nPeople are the same. Lines and calluses are evidence that someone lived alongside you.\nTonight, when you look in the mirror, do not hunt for faults. Just say one thing to yourself: these years, thank you for carrying me.'
},

'后悔当初、总想"如果当时"':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。后悔最费人的地方，是你拿今天才知道的事，去审判当年什么都不知道的自己。那时的你，手上只有那点信息。先把一句"我当时也不容易"还给他。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. What drains you in regret is that you judge the self of back then with what you only learned later. That version of you had only the information in hand. Give him this one sentence: I was not having an easy time either.',
  dharma:'有位师父带徒弟走夜路。徒弟一直回头，说刚才那条路该走左边。\n师父说：你现在站的地方，是那条路把你送来的；你回头骂它，它也不会动。\n徒弟问：那怎么办。师父说：往前走，路还在前头。\n把那件旧事里的经验拿走，别的留给过去。\n今晚写一句"从这件事里我学到什么"，写完就合上本子。',
  dharmaEn:'A teacher once walked a night road with his student. The student kept looking back, saying they should have taken the left fork.\nThe teacher said: the ground you stand on now is where that road brought you. Scold it all you like, and it will not move.\nThe student asked: then what. The teacher said: go forward — the road is still ahead.\nTake one lesson out of that old thing, and leave the rest to the past.\nTonight, write one line: what did I learn from this. Then close the notebook.'
},

'工作没有价值感、上班没意义':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。上班没意义，很多时候不是工作坏了，是你每天做的事，跟你在乎的东西没有接头。先找出你想贡献的是什么，再想怎么靠过去——而不是在难受的那一周裸辞。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Meaningless work often does not mean the job is broken; it means what you do each day never connects with what you care about. Name what you want to contribute, then plan how to move toward it — instead of quitting in a bad week.',
  dharma:'寺里有个小和尚，天天扫地，扫得烦。\n他问师父：扫地有什么用？师父说：你说的"用"，是指扫完有人夸你吗？\n小和尚说不上来。师父说：地干净了，走过去的人脚上不带泥。\n你手上的活，也常看不见落点。\n今天挑一件事，做的时候想着"谁会因为这件小事顺一点"，做完就放下。',
  dharmaEn:'In a monastery there was a young monk who swept the floor every day and grew tired of it.\nHe asked his teacher: what use is sweeping? The teacher said: when you say "use", do you mean whether someone praises you when it is done?\nThe young monk had no answer. The teacher said: the floor is clean, and whoever walks over it carries no mud on their feet.\nThe work in your hands often shows no result you can see.\nToday, pick one task and do it thinking of who will go a little easier because of it. Then set it down.'
},

'作息紊乱、黑白颠倒、想改改不过来':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。黑白颠倒这件事，靠下决心是改不过来的——身体认的是早晨的光，不是你的意志。先把起床时间固定住一周，别的，等它稳了再说。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. A reversed day and night will not be fixed by deciding harder — the body answers to morning light, not to willpower. Fix your waking time for one week first, and leave the rest until that holds.',
  dharma:'高原上白天短，人都懂得早点起。\n太阳一出来，屋里的冰自己就化了；太阳落下去，再多的柴也顶不住一夜。\n身体也是这样，它认的是光，不是决心。\n今晚不要求自己早睡，只把明天的闹钟定在同一个点。\n起床后到窗前站五分钟，让光进来。连着几天，晚上自己会困。',
  dharmaEn:'On the plateau the days are short, and everyone knows to rise early.\nWhen the sun comes up, the ice in the room melts on its own. After sunset, no amount of firewood holds off a whole night.\nThe body is the same. It answers to light, not to resolve.\nTonight, do not demand that you sleep early. Just set tomorrow’s alarm at the same hour.\nStand by the window for five minutes after you get up and let the light in. After a few days, evening will come to you on its own.'
},

'拖延、拖到最后一刻、计划总破功':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。拖到最后一刻，不是在躲事，多半是在躲"开始那一下"的不舒服。别跟整件事较劲，把开头缩到两分钟，允许自己只做这两分钟。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Leaving things to the last minute is usually not avoiding the task — it is avoiding the discomfort of starting. Do not wrestle with the whole thing. Shrink the opening to two minutes and let yourself do only those two.',
  dharma:'有个小和尚要搬一堆石头，站在那儿看了半天，一块也没动。\n师父过来，捡起一块，放到墙根，说：一块。\n小和尚笑了，也捡起一块。半天就搬完了。\n你手上的事也是这样，难的是第一块。\n今晚只做两分钟：把文件打开，写第一行。写完这两分钟就算完成。',
  dharmaEn:'A young monk was told to move a pile of stones. He stood there looking at it a long while and moved not one.\nThe teacher came over, picked up a single stone, set it by the wall, and said: one.\nThe young monk laughed and picked up one too. By afternoon the pile was gone.\nYour task works the same way. The hard part is the first stone.\nTonight, do only two minutes: open the file and write the first line. Once those two minutes are done, you are finished for today.'
},

'害怕做决定、选择困难':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。选择难，往往是因为你把每个决定都当成了不能回头的。可大部分决定是可以改的。给决定定个期限，只留两条真正重要的标准，然后选那个"够好"的。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Choosing is hard when you treat every decision as one you can never undo — and most can be undone. Give the decision a deadline, keep only the two criteria that really matter, and take the good-enough option.',
  dharma:'有个赶路人站在岔路口，坐了一上午。\n过来一位老人，他问：哪条路好？老人说：你站在这儿，两条都到不了。\n他又问：哪条近？老人说：走错了再回来，也比坐着强。\n你手上那个决定，先分清哪些能回头、哪些不能。\n今晚给能回头的那个定个期限：明天中午之前，选一个够好的。',
  dharmaEn:'A traveler stood at a fork and sat there all morning.\nAn old man came by. The traveler asked: which road is better? The old man said: standing here, neither of them will get you there.\nHe asked again: which is shorter? The old man said: walking the wrong way and coming back still beats sitting.\nSort the decision in your hands: which part can turn back, and which cannot.\nTonight, give the reversible one a deadline. By noon tomorrow, take the good-enough choice.'
},

'亲人离世、走不出来':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。这种走不出来，不是你不肯放，是你在疼。哀伤本来就不按时程表走。今天就做一件最小的：照常吃一顿饭，或者把他们的名字说出来一次。要是日子一直转不动，去找个人聊聊。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. This inability to move on is not you refusing to let go — it is you hurting. Grief keeps no timetable. Today, do the smallest thing: eat one ordinary meal, or say their name out loud once. And if daily life stops turning, go talk to someone.',
  dharma:'我认识一个老人，儿子走得早。他每天早上还是摆两副碗筷。\n有人劝他别摆了，他说：我不摆给他吃，我摆给我自己——让我记得我是有儿子的人。\n别人就没再劝。\n他们不会从你的生命里消失，只是换了个位置待着。\n今晚把他最爱吃的那样东西做一次，或者把他常说的一句话写下来。',
  dharmaEn:'I knew an old man whose son died young. Every morning he still set out two bowls.\nPeople told him to stop. He said: I do not set it out for him to eat. I set it out for myself — so I remember I am a man who had a son.\nNobody said anything after that.\nThey do not disappear from your life. They only change place in it.\nTonight, cook the dish he loved most, or write down one thing he used to say.'
},

'家人重病临终、要不要救、怎么告别':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。这样的抉择，不该你一个人在走廊里做决定。先问清医生：还能治到什么程度、怎么让他少受罪，也问问病人自己想要什么。想说的话，今天就说了。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. This is not a decision to make alone in a corridor. Ask the doctors plainly: how far can treatment go, and how can his suffering be eased. Ask what the patient himself wants. And say the words you want to say today.',
  dharma:'佛经里说，有位比丘病重，弟子们围着哭。\n他反倒劝他们：别忙着我死以后的事，先扶我坐起来，我想看看外面那棵树。\n看完，他才安安静静地走。\n我们能替人做的最要紧的事，常常不是把他留住，是让他少疼一点、想见的人见完。\n今晚别一个人扛着所有决定，把家里人叫到一起，把医生的话说给他们听。',
  dharmaEn:'The scriptures tell of a monk who was gravely ill, with his students gathered around him weeping.\nHe told them instead: do not busy yourselves with what happens after I die. Help me sit up first — I want to look at that tree outside.\nWhen he had looked, he passed quietly.\nThe most important thing we can do for someone is often not to hold them here, but to let them hurt less and see the people they want to see.\nTonight, do not carry every decision alone. Gather the family and read them what the doctor said.'
},

'怕死、一想到死就心慌':{
  compassion:'怕死不是懦弱，是知道自己珍贵。修行人不叫你不想死，只叫你别装着自己不会死：把今天当今天用，该说的话今天就说了。心慌到吃不下睡不着，就去看医生——修心不代替看病。',
  compassionEn:'Fear of death is not weakness; it means you know life is precious. We do not ask you to stop thinking of death, only to stop pretending you will not die: use today as today, and say today what should be said. If the fear takes away food and sleep, see a doctor — practice does not replace medical care.',
  dharma:'我师父晚年常说一句：秋天的叶子掉下来，不是树不要它了。\n我问他：那为什么还掉？他说：叶子在树上待了一季，该给的都给了，剩下的就是落下来。\n他走的那天很平常，早上还喝了一碗粥。\n你不用今天就想通这件事，只是别再把它当成一件不能提的事。\n今晚睡前想一想：如果只剩一年，你最想跟谁说一句话。明天就去说。',
  dharmaEn:'My teacher used to say one thing in his later years: when an autumn leaf falls, it is not because the tree no longer wants it.\nI asked him: then why does it fall? He said: the leaf stayed a season and gave what it had to give. What is left is to fall.\nThe day he died was an ordinary day. He had a bowl of porridge that morning.\nYou do not have to understand this today. Only stop treating it as something that cannot be mentioned.\nTonight before sleep, ask yourself: if I had one year left, who is the one person I would want to speak to. Then speak to them tomorrow.'
},

'确诊重病、怕时日不多':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。刚拿到结果那段日子，人的心是散的，这很正常。先把问题问清楚：治疗目标是什么、难受了怎么处理、要不要带上一个人去看门诊。日子先切成短的过，一天一天来。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. In the first days after the result, the mind scatters — that is normal. Get the questions clear first: what is the aim of treatment, what can be done about discomfort, and should you bring someone to the appointments. Take life in short pieces, one day at a time.',
  dharma:'有位老修行病了很久。人家问他怕不怕，他说：我只管今天这顿药、今天这碗饭、今天来看我的这个人。\n别人说他心大。他说：不是心大，是想远了也没用。\n你现在也是这样。医生管治疗，家人管陪着，你只管今天。\n今晚只做一件事：把明天要问医生的三个问题写在纸上。',
  dharmaEn:'An old practitioner had been ill a long time. Someone asked if he was afraid. He said: I only mind today’s medicine, today’s bowl of rice, and whoever comes to see me today.\nThey said he was carefree. He said: not carefree. Thinking far ahead just does not help.\nThat is where you are too. The doctors handle treatment, the family handles company, and you handle today.\nTonight, do one thing: write the three questions you want to ask the doctor tomorrow.'
},

'怕父母变老、怕他们离开':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。这份怕，其实是爱没有出口。别拿它去预演那一天——把它变成时间：问问他们的身体和心愿，把他们的故事记下来，让今天就是普通的一天。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. This fear is love with nowhere to go. Do not spend it rehearsing that day — turn it into time: ask about their health and their wishes, record their stories, and let today be an ordinary day.',
  dharma:'我见过一个人，天天担心母亲哪天会走。\n他妈八十了，爱包饺子。他每次回家都抢着包，怕她累着。\n有一天老太太说：你别包了，让我包，我包一次少一次。\n他后来就坐在旁边看，一边看一边把她的手法记下来。\n今晚给家里打个电话，别问完"身体好吗"就完了，问他一件你小时候的事。',
  dharmaEn:'I knew a man who worried every day that his mother would die.\nShe was eighty and loved making dumplings. He would rush to wrap them himself so she would not tire.\nOne day she said: let me do it. Each time I make them, there is one less time.\nAfter that he sat beside her and watched, memorizing how her hands moved.\nTonight, call home. Do not stop at "are you well". Ask about one thing from when you were small.'
},

'养老焦虑、怕老无所依':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。养老这件事，光焦虑是安排不出来的——它得拆成几件具体的事：钱、住哪儿、谁来照应、身体怎么维持。这个月先动一件，别想着一次想完。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Worry alone will not arrange your later years — it has to be broken into concrete pieces: money, where you will live, who can help, and how to keep your body going. Start one of them this month, not all at once.',
  dharma:'高原上入冬前，家家都要做一件事：修屋顶、备柴。\n有位老人做得最细，别人问他急什么。他说：不是怕冬天，是冬天来的时候我不想慌。\n他也没想把所有事都备齐，只把最要紧的几样弄好。\n养老也是这个道理，不是算清一切，是别让自己在冷天里手忙脚乱。\n这个月只动一件：把养老金或者医保的事，打一个电话问清楚。',
  dharmaEn:'On the plateau, before winter comes, every household does one thing: repair the roof and store firewood.\nOne old man did it most carefully. People asked why he was in a hurry. He said: it is not that I fear winter. It is that I do not want to panic when winter arrives.\nHe never tried to prepare for everything — only the few things that mattered.\nYour later years work the same way. It is not about calculating everything; it is about not being caught unready in the cold.\nThis month, do one thing: make one call about your pension or insurance and get it clear.'
},

'房价下跌、买房被套、亏了怎么办':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。账面亏了是事实，但恐慌卖出，仍是一个你可以不做的决定。先算清真实数字：月供、收入、还能撑几年；再问自己一句，这套房子还适合现在的生活吗。想清楚之前，别急着挂牌。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. A paper loss is a fact, but panic selling is still a decision you can decline to make. Get the real numbers first: the monthly payment, your income, how many years you could hold on. Then ask whether this home still fits your life now. Do not list it before you know.',
  dharma:'集市上有人买青稞，买贵了，回家一路骂自己。\n他妻子说：你已经背回来了，再骂一遍，青稞不会变便宜，你倒多累一趟。\n他问那怎么办。妻子说：算算够吃到什么时候，不够就想想明年种什么。\n亏掉的那笔钱，就是那袋青稞。\n今晚把月供、收入、还能撑的月份写在一张纸上，写完再决定要不要动。',
  dharmaEn:'At the market a man bought barley at too high a price, and cursed himself all the way home.\nHis wife said: you have already carried it back. Cursing again will not make it cheaper — it only costs you a second trip.\nHe asked what to do. She said: count how long it will feed us. If it will not last, think about what to plant next year.\nThe money you lost is that sack of barley.\nTonight, write three figures on one sheet: the monthly payment, your income, and how many months you could hold. Decide after that.'
},

'贷款逾期、断供、被催收快撑不住了':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。这种电话一天接几个，人真的会撑不住。但你不用一个人扛，也别躲着不接：先找正规的债务咨询或者法律援助，问清楚能怎么谈。钱的事再急，也不值得拿命去还。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. When the calls come several times a day, a person really does start to come apart. But you do not have to carry this alone, and you do not have to go silent: find legitimate debt counseling or legal aid and ask what can be negotiated. However urgent the money is, it is never worth your life.',
  dharma:'有个挑夫欠了债，天天躲债主。\n后来他去找债主，说：我现在还不上，我一个月能还多少，你记着。\n债主愣了愣，说：你早说啊。\n从那以后，他反倒睡得着了。\n债是债，命是命，先把这两样分开。\n今晚做一件具体的事：明天上午，主动给一家机构打个电话，或者去做一次免费的债务咨询。',
  dharmaEn:'A porter owed money and spent his days dodging his creditor.\nEventually he went to him and said: I cannot pay it all now. Here is what I can pay each month — write it down.\nThe creditor blinked and said: why did you not say so earlier.\nAfter that, the porter could sleep.\nThe debt is the debt. Your life is your life. Keep the two apart.\nTonight, do one concrete thing: tomorrow morning, call one institution yourself, or go to one free debt consultation.'
},

'要不要生孩子、不敢生':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。这个决定是你和伴侣的，不是周围人催出来的。把"我想要"和"我害怕"分开写：想要什么，怕的是钱、是身体，还是失去自己。写完再看，答案会清楚一点。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. This decision belongs to you and your partner, not to the people pushing you. Write "what I want" and "what I fear" on separate lines: what you want, and whether the fear is money, your body, or losing yourself. The answer gets clearer after that.',
  dharma:'有人问师父：我该不该成家、要不要孩子。\n师父说：你先看看山下的路，哪一条是你自己走的，哪一条是别人替你指的。\n他说：都是别人指的。师父说：那你先把别人的手指头搬开，再站一会儿。\n没有一条路是没有风险的，也没有哪一种人生因此就完整。\n今晚别急着决定，先写下三件你真正舍不得放弃的事。',
  dharmaEn:'Someone asked a teacher: should I marry, should I have children.\nThe teacher said: go look at the roads below the mountain. Which one have you walked yourself, and which one did others point out for you?\nHe said: they were all pointed out. The teacher said: then move their fingers aside for a while, and stand there a bit longer.\nNo path is without risk, and no single life script makes a person complete.\nTonight, do not decide yet. Write down three things you would truly hate to give up.'
},

'考试压力大、怕考不上、升学焦虑':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。考前心慌、睡不着，说明你把这一次看得很重，不是你不争气。复习靠结构不靠熬：固定时段加上真正的休息，再按时间做一遍模拟。分数测的是一次表现，测不出你这个人。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Panicking before an exam and losing sleep means you are taking this seriously, not that you are weak. Revision runs on structure, not on staying up: fixed study blocks with real breaks, and one timed rehearsal. A score measures one performance, not the person.',
  dharma:'我学射箭时总瞄不准，老师让我别盯着靶心。\n他说：你盯的是结果，手就僵了。看你的呼吸、看你的手，箭自己会走。\n我照做了，中不中反倒没那么揪心。\n考试也是这个：你能管的只有今天这几个钟头和手上的这支笔。\n今晚把明天的复习分成三段，每段四十分钟，中间站起来走两分钟。',
  dharmaEn:'When I was learning archery I could never aim straight. My teacher told me to stop staring at the bullseye.\nHe said: you are staring at the result, so your hands go stiff. Watch your breath and your hands, and the arrow will go on its own.\nI did that, and whether it hit mattered less.\nExams work the same way. All you control is these few hours today and the pen in your hand.\nTonight, split tomorrow’s revision into three blocks of forty minutes, and stand up and walk for two minutes between them.'
},

'反复想一件事、反复检查、洁癖强迫':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。反复冒出来的念头，不是你坏，也不等于你会去做。检查能换来几分钟安心，却让这个圈更牢。别硬扛，改成延迟十分钟再做。这件事值得找精神科或心理治疗问一次。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Thoughts that keep coming back do not mean you are bad, and they do not mean you will act on them. Checking buys a few minutes of relief and makes the loop tighter. Do not fight it — delay it ten minutes instead. This is worth one proper assessment with a doctor or therapist.',
  dharma:'有位师父教人打坐。\n学生说：我一坐，杂念就更多。师父问：你是想赶走它们吗？他说是。\n师父说：赶也是动作，你越赶，它们越知道你在。\n学生问：那怎么办。师父说：看见它来了，说一句"你来了"，再回到呼吸。\n那个想检查的冲动也这样待它：看见，招呼一声，先不回手。今晚先等十分钟。',
  dharmaEn:'A teacher was showing a student how to sit in meditation.\nThe student said: as soon as I sit, there are even more thoughts. The teacher asked: you are trying to drive them out? He said yes.\nThe teacher said: driving them out is also doing something. The harder you push, the more they know you are there.\nThe student asked what to do. The teacher said: when one arrives, say "you have come", then return to the breath.\nTreat that urge to check the same way: notice it, greet it, and do not answer it right away. Tonight, wait ten minutes first.'
},

'突然心跳很快、喘不上气、感觉要死了':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。发作那几分钟是真的吓人，但它本身不危险。先排查一次身体原因；发作时把呼气放慢，留在原地别跑，让这一波过去。反复发作，就找医生和心理治疗一起看。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Those few minutes are genuinely frightening, but the surge itself is not dangerous. Have physical causes checked once. During an attack, slow your out-breath, stay where you are instead of running, and let the wave pass. If it keeps happening, see a doctor and a therapist together.',
  dharma:'我在海边待过一阵。\n浪来的时候很吓人，一次比一次高。有经验的人不跟它顶，只往后退两步，等它自己碎掉。\n他跟我说：浪不会一直立着不动。\n你身上那阵心慌也是浪。第一次来，该找医生确认就去；确认过了，就学着站在原地等它碎。\n今晚练一个动作：呼气比吸气长一倍，数十次。',
  dharmaEn:'I spent some time by the sea.\nThe waves came in frighteningly, each one higher than the last. The people who knew the water did not push against them — they stepped back two paces and waited for the wave to break itself.\nOne of them told me: a wave cannot stand there forever.\nThat surge in your body is a wave too. The first time, let a doctor check; once that is done, learn to stand and wait for it to break.\nTonight, practise one thing: make your out-breath twice as long as your in-breath, and count ten.'
},

'压力一大就胃疼头疼、身上各种不舒服':{
  compassion:'身体在替你说心说不出口的话。别怪它不争气，先问它一句：这几个月，你替我扛了什么没说出口的？有个笨办法：吸气时把这份闷收进来，呼气时送出去一点松。难受不散，该查还得查。',
  compassionEn:'The body is saying what the heart could not say out loud. Do not blame it for being weak; ask it: what have you carried for me, unspoken, these months? Here is a clumsy method: breathe in that heaviness, and breathe out a little ease. If it does not pass, still get it checked.',
  dharma:'我有个笨办法，是在灶上学的。\n锅里的水烧开了，你压着锅盖没用，得把火收小一点，或者掀开一道缝，让它冒出来。\n身上那些疼、闷、胃里堵着的那口气，就是这股要出来的气。\n今晚给自己十五分钟：热水泡脚，或者出门走两圈，让这口气有个出口。\n走路的时候，吸气收进来，呼气把它送出去。',
  dharmaEn:'I learned a clumsy method at the stove.\nWhen the water in the pot boils, holding the lid down does nothing. You turn the fire down, or you lift the lid a crack and let it out.\nThe pain, the tightness, the air stuck in your stomach — that is steam with nowhere to go.\nTonight, give yourself fifteen minutes: soak your feet in hot water, or walk two laps outside and let it out.\nAs you walk, breathe it in, and breathe it out.'
},

'一有压力就暴食、情绪性进食管不住嘴':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。压力一上来就想吃，多半是在找一点安抚，不是你没自制力。先把三餐吃稳，别让自己饿到极点；想吃之前先停一分钟，给那个感觉起个名字。要是越来越失控，去找专业的人聊聊。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Reaching for food when pressure rises is usually a search for comfort, not a lack of discipline. Steady your three meals so you are never starving, pause for one minute before eating, and give the feeling a name. If it gets more out of control, talk to a professional.',
  dharma:'有个师父带徒弟行脚，走了很远。\n徒弟喊饿，师父从怀里掏出糌粑，先给他一小块，再让他走一段，再给一小块。\n徒弟问：为什么不一次给我？师父说：一次给你，你吃着香，走两步又饿，还想再要。\n一小块一小块，你才知道自己在吃什么。\n今晚试试：想吃的时候，先吃一小口，停一下。吃完那口，再决定给不给下一口。',
  dharmaEn:'A teacher once walked a long way with his student. The student complained of hunger. The teacher took barley flour from his bag, gave him one small piece, had him walk another stretch, then gave another small piece.\nThe student asked: why not give it all at once? The teacher said: if I give it all at once, it tastes good, and two steps later you are hungry again and want more.\nOne small piece at a time, and you know what you are eating.\nTonight, try this: when you want to eat, take one small bite first, then pause. After that bite, decide whether to take the next.'
},

'原生家庭的伤总在重演、总重复父母的相处模式':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。那些老模式会重演，不是你没长进，是因为它太熟了——熟到身体先替你反应完，你才发觉。别急着骂自己，先认出它：这个反应，是妈妈的，还是你自己的？',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. These old patterns repeat, not because you have not grown, but because they are so familiar — familiar enough that your body reacts before you even notice. Do not turn on yourself. Recognize it first: is this reaction my mother’s, or my own?',
  dharma:'我小时候学走路，是学着大人的样子走的。\n后来有人问我：你走路为什么左边肩膀低？我说不知道。\n他让我站直了走一段，我才觉出来，那是跟我父亲学的。\n学来的东西，是可以重学的。\n今晚先做一件事：写下你最常听见的那句话，再写一句你自己想说的。',
  dharmaEn:'When I was small I learned to walk by copying the grown-ups.\nYears later someone asked me: why is your left shoulder lower when you walk? I said I did not know.\nHe had me stand straight and walk a stretch, and I felt it — it was my father’s way.\nWhat was learned can be learned again.\nTonight, do one thing: write down the sentence you heard most often, then write one sentence of your own.'
},

'回避型依恋、喜欢一个人又想逃':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。想逃不是冷血，是你学会了先保护自己。它不用一次改掉：下次想消失之前，先说一句话——"我要缓一缓，不是要结束"。说完再退开，对方就知道门还开着。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Wanting to run is not coldness; it is how you learned to protect yourself. It does not have to change all at once. Next time you want to disappear, say one sentence first — "I need a pause, not an ending." Then step back, and the other person knows the door is still open.',
  dharma:'高原的冬天，人进屋第一件事是把门关上。\n有位师父说：关门是为了保暖，可你得留条缝，不然屋里的人以为你不回来了。\n有人问他：我怕冷怎么办。他说：先留缝，再慢慢加柴。\n你那个"想消失一阵"的习惯也是这样。\n今晚试试：告诉那个人你要缓三天，三天后回来说句话。',
  dharmaEn:'In the mountains in winter, the first thing anyone does indoors is shut the door.\nA teacher said: shutting it keeps the warmth in, but you have to leave a crack — otherwise the people inside think you are not coming back.\nSomeone asked him: what if I am cold? He said: leave the crack first, then add wood slowly.\nThat habit of vanishing for a while works the same way.\nTonight, try this: tell that person you need three days, and that you will come back and talk.'
},

'高敏感、心思重、总在意别人的脸色和话':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。敏感不是毛病，是你收进来的东西比旁人多。问题不在敏感，在你把猜的当成了真的。今天试着核一次事实：那句话，是真的冲着你，还是你自己补上去的？',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Being sensitive is not a defect; it means you take in more than others do. The problem is not the sensitivity, it is that you treat a guess as a fact. Today, check one thing: was that remark really aimed at you, or did you add it yourself?',
  dharma:'我这两个茶碗，一个厚一个薄。倒开水，厚的没声，薄的一倒就响。\n我问做碗的人哪个好。他说：薄的那个出香，烫得也快，你得先温一下碗。\n敏感的人就是这样，香得快，也烫得快。\n今晚只做一件：回到家先给自己十分钟安静，不做决定，也不复盘白天那句话。',
  dharmaEn:'I have two tea bowls here, one thick and one thin. Pour boiling water in, and the thick one says nothing, while the thin one rings at once.\nI asked the potter which was better. He said: the thin one gives you the fragrance, and it also heats fast — you have to warm it first.\nThat is how it is for sensitive people. Quick to bring out the fragrance, quick to burn.\nTonight, do one thing: give yourself ten quiet minutes when you get home. Decide nothing, and do not replay that remark from today.'
},

'完美主义、对自己太苛刻':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。做到一百分才肯放过自己，这不是高标准，是把标准架在了自己脖子上。试着换个说法：先做完，再做好。今天的活儿，先写清"到什么程度就算完"。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Not letting yourself off the hook until it is a hundred percent is not a high standard — it is a standard held at your throat. Try another wording: finish first, then improve. Today, write down what "done" means for the thing in front of you.',
  dharma:'我见过一位抄经的老人，字不算工整，可他一写就是二十年。\n有人问他：不怕写坏？他说：写坏了就重写一张，纸便宜，人贵。\n他给我看一叠写坏的纸，说：这些才是我的手艺。\n你今晚只做一件：给手上的事定一条"够好"的线，到了就交。',
  dharmaEn:'I knew an old man who copied scriptures. His characters were not neat, but he had done it for twenty years.\nSomeone asked: are you not afraid of ruining it? He said: if I ruin it, I write another sheet. Paper is cheap; people are not.\nHe showed me a stack of ruined sheets and said: these are my craft.\nTonight, do one thing: draw a line for "good enough" on the task in your hands, and hand it in when you reach it.'
},

'恐婚、一想到结婚就害怕想逃':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。一想到结婚就想逃，不是你不爱他，多半是有些具体的事你还没敢问：钱怎么管、边界在哪、要不要孩子、吵架怎么办。怕，常常是因为不清楚。今天挑一件问清楚。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Wanting to run at the thought of marriage usually does not mean you do not love him. It often means there are concrete things you have not dared to ask: how money will work, where the boundaries are, children or not, how you fight. Fear often comes from not knowing. Ask about one of them today.',
  dharma:'高原上盖房子，先看梁，不看墙。\n有位老人说：墙刷得再白，梁歪了，屋子住不长；梁正，墙旧点也能住一辈子。\n有个年轻人要成亲，来问他该看什么。老人说：别看他家摆了多少件家具，看他家遇上难事时怎么说话。\n今晚先跟你那位说一件实际的：钱，或者父母，或者孩子。',
  dharmaEn:'On the plateau, when a house is built, the first thing they look at is the beam, not the walls.\nAn old man said: paint the walls as white as you like — if the beam is crooked, the house will not last. If the beam is true, old walls will hold a lifetime.\nA young man came to ask what to look for in marriage. The old man said: do not count the furniture in his house. Watch how that family talks when trouble comes.\nTonight, raise one practical thing with your partner: money, or parents, or children.'
},

'孕期焦虑、怀孕后总担心想哭':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。怀孕时又哭又怕，不是你想太多，是激素、身体和身份的变动一起压过来。产检时把担心一条条问医生，别在深夜靠搜索给自己下结论。情绪一直低、睡不着，请做一次围产期心理评估。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Crying and fearing while pregnant is not you overthinking; hormones, body changes, and a change of identity all press in at once. Write your worries down and ask the doctor about each one at your next check-up instead of diagnosing yourself by search at midnight. If the low mood and sleeplessness persist, get a perinatal mental health assessment.',
  dharma:'佛经里有个比喻，说母亲抱着孩子过河。\n河水急，她只做一件事：把孩子抱稳，脚下一步一步探着走。\n她不想"能不能过去"这种问不完的问题，她只想下一块石头在哪。\n你现在也是这样。医生管检查，家人管陪着，你只管今天这顿饭、这一觉。\n今晚把担心的三件事写在纸上，明天拿去医院问。',
  dharmaEn:'The scriptures have an image of a mother carrying her child across a river.\nThe water is swift, and she does only one thing: hold the child steady, and feel for the next stone under her feet.\nShe does not ask the endless question of whether she will make it. She asks where the next stone is.\nThat is where you are. The doctors handle the tests, the family handles company, and you handle today’s meal and today’s sleep.\nTonight, write your three worries on a sheet and take it to the hospital tomorrow.'
},

'备孕很久怀不上、久备不孕压力大':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。每个月失望一次，那份累不比别的少，你们俩都在扛。别让这件事成了唯一的话题：给"谈它"设个时限，尽早做正规评估，让夫妻关系比这个目标更大一点。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. One disappointment a month takes more out of you than anyone sees, and both of you are carrying it. Do not let it become the only thing you talk about: set a limit on how much time it gets, get a proper evaluation early, and keep the relationship bigger than the goal.',
  dharma:'山里种地的人有个规矩：地要轮着歇。\n有人问：歇一年不是少收一季？老农说：一块地年年种，土就瘦了；歇一年，第二年才长得起来。\n他也不是不着急，他只是不等着一季。\n你们现在就像那块地，要按医生的安排走，也得让心里有空的时候。\n今晚先立一个小规矩：吃饭时不谈孩子的事。',
  dharmaEn:'Farmers in the mountains have a rule: land must rest in turn.\nSomeone asked: does resting a year not cost a harvest? The old farmer said: plant the same field year after year and the soil thins out. Let it rest a year, and the next year it can grow.\nHe was not unanxious. He simply did not measure by one season.\nYou two are that field right now. Follow what the doctors arrange, and let your hearts have some empty time too.\nTonight, set one small rule: no talk about children at meals.'
},

'离婚带娃、单亲妈妈/爸爸怕养不好孩子':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。孩子要的是一个稳定的大人，不是一个完美的家庭形状。你不需要同时当两个人：把日常弄得可预期，别让孩子替大人传话，也给自己找点实际的帮手。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. What a child needs is one steady adult, not the perfect shape of a family. You do not have to be two parents at once: make daily life predictable, keep the child out of grown-up conflict, and arrange some real help for yourself.',
  dharma:'有人挑着担子过独木桥，一边一个筐。他怕偏，走得发抖。\n桥头的老汉喊：别看筐，看脚下那三寸，一步一步过。\n过了桥他才发现，两边筐都好好的。\n你现在的日子就是那座桥，两边都要顾，可你能看的只有脚下这一步。\n今晚安排一件具体的帮手：让谁哪天接一次孩子。',
  dharmaEn:'A man crossed a narrow wooden bridge carrying a shoulder pole with a basket on each end. Afraid of tipping, he shook all the way.\nAn old man at the bridge shouted: do not look at the baskets. Look at the three inches under your feet, one step at a time.\nWhen he was across, both baskets were fine.\nYour days are that bridge now. The child and you both need looking after, but the only part you can see is the next step.\nTonight, arrange one concrete helper: who picks up the child on which day.'
},

'职场被领导PUA、当众贬低打压':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。被反复当众贬低，是真的会让人开始怀疑自己的。但那是职场的问题，不是关于你的证明。先做两件事：把时间、原话记下来；把"你不行"这三个字，拿去跟一个信得过的人核一核。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Being put down in front of others again and again will genuinely make you start doubting yourself. But that is a workplace problem, not evidence about you. Do two things first: write down the dates and the actual words; and take that "you are no good" to one person you trust and check it against them.',
  dharma:'我见过一棵长在墙边的树。墙那边的院子大，树长得最好的一半都在墙外。\n站在墙内的人说：这树长得歪。\n种树的人只回了一句：你看的那一面，不是它全部的样子。\n有人只看你哪一面，不代表你就是那一面。\n今晚做一件小事：把这阵子被贬低的事，按日期写三行。',
  dharmaEn:'I once saw a tree growing against a wall. The yard on the other side was wide, and the best half of that tree was over the wall.\nPeople standing inside the wall said: that tree grows crooked.\nThe one who planted it said only: the side you are looking at is not all of it.\nSomeone seeing one side of you does not make you that side.\nTonight, do one small thing: write three lines, with dates, of the times you were put down.'
},

'孩子厌学、不肯上学、休学在家':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。孩子不去学校，通常不是懒，是有东西卡住了——被欺负、听不懂、或者心里太慌。先别逼问，也别急着讲道理，把这当成需要专业帮忙的事：找学校，也找心理医生看看。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. A child who will not go to school is usually not lazy; something is stuck — bullying, not understanding the class, or too much fear inside. Do not interrogate and do not rush to lecture. Treat this as something needing professional help: talk to the school, and see a child psychologist.',
  dharma:'我见过一只猫，从房梁上下来，卡在树上下不去。\n我们在树下喊它、拿吃的逗它，它越躲越高。后来我们走开，把一碗鱼放在树底下，各自去干活。\n那碗鱼摆了两天，它自己下来了。\n孩子现在就在那棵树上。先成为他敢下来时还在的那个人。\n今晚只做一件：跟他说一句"什么时候想说，我都在"，别追问。',
  dharmaEn:'I once saw a cat climb down from a roof beam and get stuck in a tree.\nWe called to it and waved food, and it climbed higher. So we walked away and left a bowl of fish at the foot of the tree, and went back to work.\nThe bowl sat there two days, and then it came down on its own.\nYour child is up that tree right now. Be the person who is still there when he dares to come down.\nTonight, do one thing: tell him "whenever you want to talk, I am here", and then do not press.'
},

'身材容貌焦虑、总觉得自己不好看':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。照镜子越久，毛病找得越多，这不是你难看，是你的眼睛被训练得只会挑错。今天少做两次：少照一次镜子，少修一张图。把身体当成干活的伙伴，而不是等着打分的展品。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. The longer you stand at the mirror, the more faults you find. That is not because you are ugly; it is because your eye has been trained to look only for flaws. Do two fewer things today: look in the mirror one time less, edit one photo fewer. Treat your body as a partner doing the work, not an exhibit waiting to be scored.',
  dharma:'高原上的山，远看各有各的样，走近了都是石头的纹路。\n有人天天嫌自己不好看。师父让他去看山。回来说：山也不好看，可谁也不嫌它。师父说：那你嫌的是谁？\n他答不上来。\n身体不是拿来评的，它带你走了这么多年。\n今晚睡前跟它说一句：今天你带我走了一天。',
  dharmaEn:'The mountains on the plateau all look different from a distance. Up close, they are all grain and stone.\nSomeone complained every day about being ugly. His teacher sent him to look at the mountains for a day. He came back and said: the mountains are not beautiful either, and no one holds it against them. The teacher said: then who are you holding it against?\nHe had no answer.\nA body is not something to be graded. It has carried you all these years.\nTonight before sleep, say one thing to it: today you carried me through the day.'
},

'在学校被孤立排挤、被同学冷落针对':{
  compassion:'来，先坐下。被排挤很疼，但它证明不了你不值得被喜欢。今天做两件事：把发生的事写下来，找一个真能管这事的大人说；在那个圈子外面，先交一个朋友。',
  compassionEn:'Come, sit down first. Being left out hurts, and it cannot prove that you are unlovable. Do two things today: write down what happened, and tell one adult who can actually act on it. Outside that circle, make one friend first.',
  dharma:'山上的树不是都长在一起。有些树自己长在坡上，风大，可它先见到太阳。\n有人问师父：我融不进他们。师父说：你先别急着融，看看你脚下这块地。\n他后来在坡上长成了一棵好树。\n你不需要所有人喜欢你，你需要一个安全的角落，和一两件拿得出手的事。\n今晚写下一件你做得好的事。明天，找那个能管事的老师说一句实话。',
  dharmaEn:'Trees on the mountain do not all grow together. Some stand alone on the slope, where the wind is hard, but they see the sun first.\nSomeone asked his teacher: I cannot fit in with them. The teacher said: do not rush to fit in. Look at the patch of ground you are standing on.\nHe grew into a good tree on that slope.\nYou do not need everyone to like you. You need one safe corner and one or two things you can do well.\nTonight, write down one thing you do well. Tomorrow, tell the teacher who can act one honest sentence.'
},

'孩子在学校被欺负、被打、被孤立，家长怎么办':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。孩子被打被欺负，你先要做的不是让他"打回去"，是让他知道你信他。不带责备地问清事实，留下伤和时间的记录，正式找学校要一个安全方案；有暴力，就报警。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. When your child is hit or bullied, what he needs first is not being told to hit back — it is knowing that you believe him. Ask about the facts without blame, keep records of injuries and dates, and formally ask the school for a safety plan. Where there is violence, call the police.',
  dharma:'高原上有一种鸟，别的鸟来抢窝时，它不扑上去撕打。\n它先做一件事：把雏鸟挡在身后，然后一直叫，叫到整片坡的同类都飞过来。\n它赢，不是因为凶，是因为它叫来了人。\n你现在要做的也是这个：先把孩子护住，再叫上能管事的人。\n今晚只做一件：写下今天发生的事、时间和伤在哪，明天带去学校。',
  dharmaEn:'On the plateau there is a bird that guards its nest. When other birds come to raid it, it does not fly at them to tear them apart.\nIt does one thing first: it puts the chicks behind it, and then it calls and calls until every one of its kind on the slope comes flying.\nIt wins not by being fierce, but by calling others in.\nThat is what you need to do now: shield the child first, then call in the people who can act.\nTonight, do one thing only: write down what happened today, the time, and where the injuries are. Take it to the school tomorrow.'
},

'总遇渣男渣女、恋爱脑上头、一谈就卑微':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。一次次撞上同样的人，不是你命不好，是你太早把全部给出去，也太晚看见信号。这次换个做法：把自己的生活和朋友留住，第一次明确越界，就走。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Landing with the same kind of person again and again is not bad fate. It is giving everything away too early and seeing the signs too late. Change one thing this time: keep your own life and friends, and leave at the first clear crossing of a line.',
  dharma:'有人问师父：为什么我总遇到不好的人。\n师父问他：你什么时候动心？他说：对方一说好听的话。\n师父说：那你等他把话说完，看他做的事再说。\n后来又有人问同样的问题，师父只说：火别一次烧尽，留点干柴看明天。\n今晚只做一件：写下三个你以前见过的、当时忽略了的信号。',
  dharmaEn:'Someone asked his teacher: why do I always meet unkind people.\nThe teacher asked: when do you fall for someone? He said: when they say something sweet.\nThe teacher said: then wait until they have finished talking, and look at what they do.\nLater someone asked the same question, and the teacher said only: do not burn all the firewood at once. Keep some dry wood for tomorrow.\nTonight, do one thing: write down three signals you saw before and ignored.'
},

'谈婚论嫁因为钱崩了：彩礼、房子、嫁妆谈不拢':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。钱谈崩了，疼的不只是钱，是发现自己在他家像一件要议价的东西。先别急着定性：把真实数字和各自的期待写在纸上，分清哪些可谈、哪些不可谈，再找一个中立的人一起说。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. When the money talks break down, what hurts is not only the money — it is discovering you are being priced in their family. Do not label everything yet: put the real numbers and each side’s expectations on paper, sort what is negotiable from what is not, then bring in one neutral person to sit with you.',
  dharma:'集市上有两个人合伙买了一张饼，切开时谁都说对方那块大。\n卖饼的掏出自己的小秤，说：你们各自称一称。\n称完谁也没话说——差的那一点，比他们吵的那半天小得多。\n钱上的争执常常也是这样：真正差的没多少，吵的是"你有没有把我当回事"。\n今晚把数字写出来，两个人各写一列，写完再谈。',
  dharmaEn:'At the market two men went shares on a flatbread. When it was cut, each said the other’s piece was bigger.\nThe seller took out his small scale and said: weigh them yourselves.\nAfter weighing, neither had anything to say — the difference was far smaller than the time they had spent arguing.\nArguments about money are often like this. What actually differs is small; what they are arguing about is whether you respect me.\nTonight, write the numbers out, both of you, one column each. Talk after that.'
},

'被家暴了、被打第一次、要不要原谅、怎么自保':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。这不是你的错，一次也不算少。先做最要紧的三件：找一个安全的地方、带上证件和钱、告诉一个信得过的人。原谅的事，等你安全了再想；撑不住就打当地求助热线，或者报警。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. This is not your fault, and once is not little. Do the three most important things first: find a safe place, take your documents and money, and tell one person you trust. Whether to forgive can wait until you are safe. If you cannot hold on, call a local hotline or the police.',
  dharma:'佛经里说，有个比丘住的山洞旁有毒蛇。\n别人劝他：你该把蛇赶走。他说：我先搬走。\n有人笑他胆小。他说：慈悲不是把手伸进蛇口里。\n你现在要做的也是——先离开那个地方。\n今晚只做一件：把证件和一点钱收在一起，放在随时能带走的地方。',
  dharmaEn:'The scriptures tell of a monk whose cave had a poisonous snake beside it.\nPeople told him: you should drive the snake away. He said: I will move out first.\nSome laughed at him for being timid. He said: compassion does not mean putting your hand into the snake’s mouth.\nThat is your task now — leave that place first.\nTonight, do one thing: put your documents and some money together somewhere you could pick up and carry out at any moment.'
},

'胎停/流产后走不出来、怕再怀又失去':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。这是一次真实的失去，没有期限，也不是你没照顾好自己。想哭就哭，不用跟谁解释。做一次医生安排的复查，也把伴侣拉进来一起待着——别一个人扛。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. This is a real loss, it keeps no timetable, and it is not because you failed to take care of yourself. Cry when you need to; you owe no one an explanation. Go to the follow-up the doctor arranges, and bring your partner into it — do not carry this alone.',
  dharma:'山里播种，十粒种子不一定都出苗。\n老农说：不是谁做错了什么，是有些种子自己没醒。\n有个妇人流了孩子，来问他是不是自己作孽。老人说：地还在，明年还能种；你先把自己养回来。\n你现在要做的就是这样：先把身体和心养回来。\n今晚允许自己什么都不做，早点睡。',
  dharmaEn:'When farmers sow in the mountains, ten seeds do not always come up.\nThe old farmer said: it is not that anyone did something wrong. Some seeds simply do not wake.\nA woman who had lost a child came to ask him whether it was her fault. The old man said: the field is still here, and next year it can be planted. First, tend yourself back.\nThat is your task now: tend your body and your heart back first.\nTonight, let yourself do nothing at all. Sleep early.'
},

'男人压力大、有苦说不出、扛不住了也不敢哭':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。话憋在心里久了，会变成睡不着、发火、喝闷酒，甚至更糟的念头。你今天只需要对一个人说一句真话。扛不住的时候打一次心理热线——那不是说你不像男人，那是给自己留条路。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Words held in too long turn into sleeplessness, outbursts, drinking, and worse thoughts. Today you only need to say one true sentence to one person. And when you cannot hold it, call a mental health line once — that does not make you less of a man, it keeps a road open for you.',
  dharma:'高原上的水渠，每隔一段要开个口子。\n老人说：不开，水会把渠冲垮。\n我问：开了不是浪费水？他说：那点水浇了旁边的地，渠才留得住。\n你这些年一直堵着，渠里已经满了。\n今晚只做一件：找一个信得过的人，说一句"我这阵子很难"。就这一句就够。',
  dharmaEn:'On the plateau, the irrigation channels have a gap opened every so often.\nAn old man said: if you do not open it, the water breaks the channel.\nI asked: does that not waste water? He said: that little bit waters the field beside it, and the channel survives.\nYou have been blocking it for years, and the channel is full.\nTonight, do one thing: find one person you trust and say "I am having a hard time". That one sentence is enough.'
},

'退休后失落、突然没事干、觉得自己没用了':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。不是你没用了，是每天叫你起床的那件事停了。角色的东西被拿走，总会疼一阵。先给这一周定个简单的骨架：几点起、去哪儿走走、跟谁见一面。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. It is not that you are useless — it is that the thing that woke you up every morning has stopped. Losing a role hurts for a while. Give the week a simple frame first: what time you get up, where you walk, who you see.',
  dharma:'山里有个赶牛的人，牛老了要卸犁。\n头几天，牛站在地里不肯走，赶也赶不回去。那人只好每天照样把它牵到地里，让它站一会儿，再牵回家。\n半个月后，牛自己开始往河边走了。\n你也刚卸了犁，别急着今天就找到新的事。\n明天按上班的点起床，出门走半小时，别的慢慢来。',
  dharmaEn:'In the mountains there was a man who drove oxen. When his ox grew old, he took the plough off.\nFor the first days the ox stood in the field and would not leave, and could not be driven home. So the man led it to the field every day, let it stand a while, then led it back.\nHalf a month later, the ox began walking to the river by itself.\nYou have only just had your plough taken off. Do not rush to find something new today.\nTomorrow, get up at your usual work hour and walk outside for half an hour. The rest can come slowly.'
},

'更年期情绪失控、莫名想哭、容易发火、潮热出汗':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。这段时间的情绪和失眠，是激素在动，不是你的脾气坏了，更不是你人变了。先去看一次医生，把潮热和睡眠处理一下；家里人也该知道，这不是你故意的。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. The moods and the sleeplessness in this stretch come from hormones shifting — it is not your temper gone bad, and you are not becoming a different person. Go and see a doctor once and deal with the hot flushes and the sleep. Your family should also know this is not on purpose.',
  dharma:'山里的天气有一段最难将就：上午晴，下午雪，晚上又化。\n老人说：这不是天不好，是换季。\n有人在那几天里骂天，天也不理他；聪明的人只是多带一件衣服。\n你现在也是换季。身体在动，家里人多担待一点，你自己多备一件"衣服"。\n今晚先做一件：把医生的话记下来，睡前两小时不开手机。',
  dharmaEn:'Mountain weather has a stretch that is hardest to live with: clear in the morning, snow in the afternoon, thawing again by night.\nThe old people say: it is not that the sky has gone bad. It is the season turning.\nSomeone who curses the sky on those days gets nothing; the sensible one just carries an extra layer.\nYou are in a turning season too. The body is moving; let the family bear with you, and keep an extra layer for yourself.\nTonight, do one thing: write down what the doctor said, and keep the phone off for two hours before bed.'
},

'信息过载、刷新闻越刷越焦虑':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。越刷越慌，是因为焦虑跟着"你查得多勤"走，不跟着"你知道多少"走。定两个时段看消息，只留两个可靠来源，睡前至少一小时不刷。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. The more you scroll, the more anxious you feel, because anxiety follows how often you check, not how much you know. Set two windows for the news, keep two reliable sources, and stop scrolling at least an hour before sleep.',
  dharma:'有人口渴，趴在河边猛喝，越喝越渴。\n旁边的人说：你别连着喝，含一口，咽下去，歇一会儿。\n他歇了歇，就不那么渴了。\n消息也是水，河一直在那儿，你不需要一次喝完整条河。\n今晚定两个时段看消息，别的钟头就把手机放远一点。',
  dharmaEn:'A man was thirsty and drank flat out from the river. The more he drank, the thirstier he got.\nSomeone beside him said: do not keep drinking straight on. Hold a mouthful, swallow, rest a while.\nHe rested, and the thirst eased.\nNews is water too. The river is always there; you do not have to drink the whole river at once.\nTonight, set two windows for checking, and put the phone further away the rest of the time.'
},

'同事冲突、不会沟通、工作关系紧张':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。跟同事别扭，大多不是人品问题，是话没说到点上。说具体的行为、不说人：哪件事、什么时候、造成什么影响，再说一句你希望怎样。一次谈一件，别攒着。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Friction with a colleague is usually not about character; it is that the words never landed on the point. Describe the specific behavior, not the person: what happened, when, what effect it had, then say what you would like. One issue at a time, and do not let it bank up.',
  dharma:'我见过两个僧人，为一个水缸放哪儿，别扭了半年。\n老和尚把缸挪开，说：你们争的是缸，还是谁该让一步？\n两人都不说话。第二天，一个先说：放你那边也行。\n先说事实，再说希望，别把"我不服"也塞进去。\n今晚写下明天要说的那两句话。',
  dharmaEn:'I once saw two monks fall out over where a water jar should stand, and stay cool with each other for half a year.\nThen the old master moved the jar aside and said: are you arguing about the jar, or about who should give way?\nNeither of them answered. The next day one spoke first: it can stand on your side.\nSay the fact, then say what you want, and leave "I am not giving in" out of it.\nTonight, write down the two sentences you will say tomorrow.'
},

'朋友渐行渐远、关系变淡':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。友情多半不是吵没的，是淡掉的——两头都等着对方先开口。今天发一条具体的消息，别说"改天聚"，就说定哪天。有些朋友属于过去的季节，也不必勉强。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Friendships usually do not die in a quarrel; they thin out, with both sides waiting for the other to speak first. Send one concrete message today. Do not say "let us meet sometime" — name a day. And some friends belong to an earlier season; you do not have to force it.',
  dharma:'有条河，早年从我们村口过，后来改了道。\n老人说：河改道不是不流了，是它去了别处。你要喝水，就走过去挑。\n有人问：那旧河床怎么办？老人说：长草，挺好。\n你那些淡了的朋友，有些走两步还能见，有些就长起草来。\n今晚只做一件：给一个人发条消息，约一个具体的日子。',
  dharmaEn:'There was a river that used to run past our village gate. Later it changed course.\nThe old people said: it did not stop flowing. It went somewhere else. If you want water, walk over and fetch it.\nSomeone asked: what about the old riverbed? The old people said: it grows grass. That is fine.\nOf those friends who have thinned out, some are two steps away, and some will grow grass.\nTonight, do one thing: message one person and name a specific day.'
},

'宠物离世、失去陪伴走不出来':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。别人说"不就是只猫狗"，你不必接这句话。一起生活了那么多年，这就是一次真实的丧亲，哭是应该的。今天可以就为它难过一会儿，不用解释。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. When people say "it was only a cat" or "only a dog", you do not have to accept that. After that many years together, this is a real bereavement, and crying is right. Today you may simply be sad about it. No explanation needed.',
  dharma:'我养过一条狗，他走了以后，我半年不敢看它睡过的那块地方。\n有位师父问我：你现在想起他，是疼，还是暖？\n我说有时候疼，有时候暖。他说：那就是他还在。\n你不用急着不想他。\n今晚做一件事：把他的一件小东西放在你看得见的地方，跟他说句话。',
  dharmaEn:'I had a dog. After he died, I could not look at the place he used to sleep for half a year.\nA teacher asked me: when you think of him now, does it hurt, or does it warm you?\nI said sometimes it hurts, sometimes it warms. He said: that means he is still here.\nYou do not have to stop missing him any time soon.\nTonight, do one thing: put one small thing of his where you can see it, and say a few words to him.'
},

'长期照顾家人、照顾者耗竭':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。照顾人的耗竭，来自没有人来照顾你。休息一次不是抛下他，是让你还能继续。把任务分到具体人头上，安排一段固定的喘息，也去问问医生有没有喘息服务。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Caregiver exhaustion comes from no one caring for the caregiver. One rest does not abandon him — it is what lets you keep going. Give other family members named tasks, arrange a fixed block of relief, and ask the doctor about respite services.',
  dharma:'我以前守夜，靠一盏酥油灯。\n有经验的人说：灯快灭了别只顾着挡风，得添油。灯灭了，屋里谁都看不见。\n你这些年一直挡风，忘了添油。\n照顾自己不是不管别人，是别让灯先灭。\n今晚只做一件：跟家人说定，哪一天哪几个小时是你自己的。',
  dharmaEn:'I used to sit up at night by a butter lamp.\nSomeone experienced told me: when the lamp is going out, do not just shield it from the wind — add oil. If the lamp dies, no one in the room can see.\nYou have spent years shielding it, and forgot to add oil.\nCaring for yourself is not neglecting him. It is keeping the lamp from dying first.\nTonight, do one thing: settle with the family which day and which hours belong to you.'
},

'搬家后不适应、新城市孤独':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。到一座新城，大半年都像借住，这很正常。别急着"融入"：先定三条固定路线，重复去同一家店，让同一批人认得你。熟悉，是靠重复长出来的。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. In a new city, the first half year feels like staying in someone else’s place. That is normal. Do not rush to "fit in": set three fixed routes, go back to the same shop, and let the same people get to know you. Familiarity grows out of repetition.',
  dharma:'山里栽树，头一年不长个儿。\n老农说：别急，它在认土。土认好了，第二年猛长。\n有人问他：怎么让它认得快点？他说：水浇在同一处，别天天挪地方。\n你刚到新地方，也是先认土。\n今晚挑一家店，明天起连着去三天，跟老板点同一碗面。',
  dharmaEn:'When a tree is planted in the mountains, it does not grow taller the first year.\nThe old farmer said: do not rush it. It is learning the soil. Once the soil is learned, it grows fast the second year.\nSomeone asked: how can you make it learn faster? He said: pour the water in the same spot, and do not keep moving it.\nYou have just arrived somewhere new. Learn the soil first.\nTonight, pick one shop and go there three days running, and order the same bowl of noodles.'
},

'怕第一印象不好、见面就失常':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。第一印象确实要紧，但它的作用跟你怕的不一样：人只记得开头那一点，你不需要一次表现全部。挑一个你要留下的印象——可靠，或者亲切——再把注意力放到"我想了解他什么"上。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. First impressions do matter, but not in the way you fear: people remember the opening most, so you do not need to show everything at once. Choose one impression to leave — reliable, or warm — and put your attention on what you want to learn about the other person.',
  dharma:'我们这儿见客，先递一碗茶。\n有年轻人问：要是茶不好，人家不就看轻我了？老师父说：茶是引子，不是考卷。你把茶递到手上，剩下的靠说话。\n见面要紧的，不是把自己摆得多好，是让对方坐得住。\n今晚准备好一句实在的开场话：说清你来做什么，或者你想问什么。',
  dharmaEn:'Where we live, when a guest comes, you hand them tea first.\nA young man asked: if the tea is poor, will they not think less of me? The old teacher said: the tea is an opening, not an exam. You put it in their hands, and the rest is in the talking.\nWhat matters in a meeting is not how well you display yourself, but whether the other person can sit at ease.\nTonight, prepare one honest opening line: say what you have come for, or what you want to ask.'
},

'容易被光环骗、看人看走眼':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。一个亮点会让人自动补全其余部分——他专业，你就以为他可靠。看人别只看一件：记三本账，答应的事做到几件、遇麻烦时怎么反应、怎么对不如他的人。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. One bright quality makes the mind fill in the rest — he is good at his work, so you assume he is trustworthy. Do not judge by one item. Keep three ledgers: how many promises were kept, how he reacts when trouble comes, and how he treats people below him.',
  dharma:'集市上买马有个规矩：先看蹄子，再看牙口，最后才看毛色。\n老人说：毛色好看的，跑起来不一定行。\n有人只挑好看的买，回家拉不动车，才知道吃了亏。\n看人也按这个顺序：先看他怎么做事、怎么待不如他的人，再看他有多亮。\n今晚写下你正在判断的这个人，做到过哪三件事。',
  dharmaEn:'At the market there is a rule for buying a horse: look at the hooves first, then the teeth, and the coat last.\nThe old man said: the one with the nicest coat does not always run well.\nSomeone bought only by looks, and found out when the horse could not pull the cart.\nJudge people in that order too: how they work, how they treat those below them, and only then how bright they are.\nTonight, write down three things the person you are weighing has actually done.'
},

'被人贴标签、被偏见定义':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。标签是对方在走捷径，不是在陈述事实。你不必收下它，也不必急着证明自己——越急着自证，越是把别人的评价接到了自己身上。今天照常做你的事，把一件具体的事做好。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. A label is the other person taking a shortcut, not a statement of fact. You do not have to accept it, and you do not have to rush to prove yourself — the harder you rush, the more you are attaching their judgment to yourself. Do your work as usual today, and do one concrete thing well.',
  dharma:'有人给师父送来一双新鞋，尺码小了。师父试了试就放下了，没多说一句话。\n徒弟问：您不生气？师父说：这不是我的脚，是那双鞋做小了。\n别人给你贴的标签，有些就是那双小鞋。\n今晚不用争，也不用证明。把它放下，穿你自己能走的鞋。',
  dharmaEn:'Someone brought the teacher a new pair of shoes. They were a size too small. He tried them and set them aside without a word.\nHis student asked: are you not angry? He said: this is not my foot. The shoes were made too small.\nSome labels people put on you are those small shoes.\nTonight, do not argue and do not prove. Set them down and wear the shoes you can walk in.'
},

'总觉得是别人的错、怪完又后悔':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。人看得见别人的行为，却清楚自己的难处，所以别人显得不靠谱，自己显得有道理。责怪之前，先把那句话换成"他可能是什么处境"，重说一遍。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. We see other people’s behavior but we know our own circumstances, so others look careless and we look reasonable. Before blaming, say that sentence again as "what might his situation be".',
  dharma:'有条路要过一条小溪。甲看到乙踩了水，溅了别人一身，就骂他不长眼。\n后来甲自己走过，才发现那块石头是活的，谁踩谁滑。\n他回头道了歉。\n你骂过的人，多半你也没走过他那段路。\n今晚先做一件：把那件让你生气的事，换成他的处境，重讲一遍给自己听。',
  dharmaEn:'A path crossed a stream. A saw B step in the water and splash someone, and called him careless.\nLater A crossed himself and found that the stone was loose — anyone who stepped on it slipped.\nHe went back and apologized.\nMost of the people you have blamed, you have never walked their stretch of road.\nTonight, do one thing: take the thing that made you angry and tell it to yourself again from his situation.'
},

'看不惯某个人、一见就有火':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。一看见就有火，这火常常是照见，不只是讨厌。把那句不满写成一句具体的话，然后问自己：这句话，能不能也说我？能，就是照见；不能，多半是边界的事。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Anger that flares the moment you see someone is usually a mirror, not just dislike. Write the complaint as one concrete sentence, then ask yourself: could this sentence also be about me? If it can, it is a mirror. If it cannot, it is probably a boundary problem.',
  dharma:'我有个早上洗脸的铜盆，擦亮了能照人。\n有段时间我总觉得盆里那张脸难看。后来发现，是我那几天没睡好。\n有位师父说：你嫌的那个人，可能是一面镜子。\n今晚写下一句你对他的不满，写具体，不带形容词。写完看看，这句像不像在说你。',
  dharmaEn:'I have a brass basin for washing my face in the morning. Polished, it reflects a person.\nFor a while I thought the face in it was ugly. Then I realized I simply had not slept well those days.\nA teacher said: the person you dislike may be a mirror.\nTonight, write down one complaint about him, concretely, without adjectives. Then see whether that sentence could be describing you.'
},

'融不进圈子、新环境谁都不认识':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。进一个新圈子，靠的不是魅力，是出现得够多次。别想着一次给人留好印象：固定时间、固定地方，跟同一批人打招呼，一次认下一个名字。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Getting into a new circle is not about charm; it is about showing up often enough. Do not try to make one strong impression: same times, same place, greet the same faces, and learn one name per visit.',
  dharma:'我们这儿有个甜茶馆，开了二十年，老板才把常来的人认全。\n有人问他：您记得住谁？他说：天天来那几个，话不多，可我一看就知道他要甜的还是要淡的。\n熟不是聊出来的，是来出来的。\n你今晚不用准备话题，只做一件：定下每周固定的时间，去同一个地方待着。',
  dharmaEn:'We have a sweet tea house here. Its owner only knows the regulars by name after twenty years.\nSomeone asked him: who do you remember? He said: the ones who come every day. They do not talk much, but I know at a glance whether they want it sweet or light.\nFamiliarity is not talked into being. It comes from coming.\nTonight you do not need topics prepared. Do one thing: fix a weekly time and go sit in the same place.'
},

'付出很多却没人记情、关系不对等':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。给得太多、大到还不起的时候，对方常常不是感激，是绕开。先问自己一句：我是在给，还是在换？如果是换，就直说要什么，别用委屈自己来付账。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. When what you give is too large to repay, people often do not feel gratitude — they avoid it. Ask yourself first: am I giving, or trading? If it is trading, say plainly what you want instead of paying with your own resentment.',
  dharma:'有人背了一筐菜送到邻居家，连送三年。\n第四年他没送，邻居问他：今年怎么没菜了？他气了一整个冬天。\n有位师父问他：你送的时候，说过你想要什么吗？他说没有。\n师父说：那不是送，那是记账。\n今晚挑一件你一直在做的事，把"我想要什么"直说一次。',
  dharmaEn:'A man carried a basket of vegetables to his neighbor’s door three years running.\nThe fourth year he did not, and the neighbor asked: no vegetables this year? He was angry the whole winter.\nA teacher asked him: when you gave them, did you ever say what you wanted? He said no.\nThe teacher said: then that was not giving. That was bookkeeping.\nTonight, pick one thing you have been doing all along, and say out loud once what you want.'
},

'越使劲越拧、怎么说都不听':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。风吹不掉大衣，暖一点它自己会解开。压力只会招来对抗。把话换一下：先说看到的事实，不下判断，一次只谈一件事，要求小到对方能答应。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Wind cannot take a coat off; a little warmth loosens it. Pressure only invites resistance. Change the wording: state the fact you saw without judging, discuss one thing at a time, and make the request small enough to say yes to.',
  dharma:'冬天在外头手冻僵了，你使劲搓，越搓越疼。\n端到火边烘一会儿，反倒自己就热了。\n老人说：冷的东西不能用力，得用暖。\n你越使劲，对方越往回缩，也是这个道理。\n今晚把要求改小一次：从"你从来不管孩子"换成"今晚你哄一次睡"。',
  dharmaEn:'When your hands are frozen numb outdoors in winter, rubbing them hard only hurts more.\nHold them near the fire a while, and the warmth comes back on its own.\nThe old people said: cold things do not yield to force. They yield to warmth.\nThe harder you push, the more the other person pulls back — the same principle.\nTonight, make one request smaller: instead of "you never look after the child", try "put him to bed once tonight".'
},

'在外面忍着、回家就炸':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。火会顺着阻力最小的路往下传：老板给你，你给家人，家人给孩子。不是家人点的那把火。进门前给自己十分钟，先把火卸掉再进去。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Anger travels the path of least resistance: the boss gives it to you, you give it to your family, your family gives it to the child. Your family did not light that fire. Give yourself ten minutes before you walk in, and set it down first.',
  dharma:'赶了一天路的人，进帐篷前有个规矩：先把驮子卸了，再进去坐。\n有人问：先坐下歇会儿不行吗？老人说：驮子不卸，你歇也是背着它歇。\n你白天背的那些气，就是驮子。\n今晚试试：到家门口先在楼下站十分钟，或者绕着楼走一圈，卸完了再上楼。',
  dharmaEn:'People who have traveled all day have a rule before entering the tent: unload the packs first, then go in and sit.\nSomeone asked: can I not sit and rest first? The old man said: if the pack is still on, you are resting with it on your back.\nThe temper you carried all day is that pack.\nTonight, try this: stand downstairs for ten minutes before going up, or walk one lap around the building, and unload before you go in.'
},

'有自伤念头、想死、觉得撑不下去了':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下，别一个人待着。这个念头现在这么重，先做一件事：打 12356（全国心理援助热线，24 小时），或 120，或马上叫一个信得过的人来陪着你。你不是矫情，是背得太久了。今晚不用想通什么，只要能过完这一夜。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down, and do not stay alone with this. If the thought is this heavy, do one thing first: call a crisis line (in mainland China, 12356, 24 hours), or emergency services, or ask someone you trust to come and stay with you. You are not being dramatic — you have carried too much for too long. Tonight you do not have to figure anything out. You only have to get through this one night.',
  dharma:'佛经里有个比喻。\n旅人在险路上走，身后有虎，前面是崖，心里只剩一个念头：完了。\n带路的人没叫他立刻想明白路在哪，只说了一句：先站到那块平地上来。\n站住了，风就不那么急，路也看得见了。\n你今晚也一样——先把能伤到自己的东西交出去，先拉住一个人的手。这不是逃，是先护住命。路等天亮再找。',
  dharmaEn:'There is an image in the scriptures.\nA traveler on a narrow path, a tiger behind him and a cliff ahead, thinks only: this is the end.\nThe guide did not ask him to work out the road. He said one thing: step onto that flat ground first.\nStanding there, the wind eased, and the road became visible.\nTonight is the same for you — hand over anything you could hurt yourself with, and hold on to one person. This is not running away. It is keeping the life. Look for the road after daylight.'
},

'被性侵、被性骚扰、不敢说':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下，先听这一句：这不是你的错。现在最要紧的是安全——骚扰还在继续，就留好证据，打 110，或找妇联 12338；身体不舒服，去正规医院查一次。再找一个人说出来，哪怕只说一句。你不用马上想开，也不用马上放下。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first, and hear this one line: it was not your fault. What matters most right now is safety — if the harassment is still going on, keep the evidence, call the police, or contact a women’s support service; if your body is hurting, get checked at a hospital. Then tell one person, even one sentence. You do not have to make sense of it yet, and you do not have to let it go yet.',
  dharma:'佛经里讲过一个人被毒箭射中。\n他疼得厉害，却先追问：箭是谁射的？什么木头？什么羽毛？\n佛陀说：先拔箭，先治伤，那些问题可以以后再说。\n你现在就是中箭的人。谁对谁错、为什么是你，都可以先放着；先把箭拔出来——看医生、留证据、找一个信得过的人。\n追责的事有人替你做，治伤的事没人能替你做。',
  dharmaEn:'The scriptures tell of a man struck by a poisoned arrow.\nIn great pain, he asked first: who shot it? What wood? What feathers?\nThe Buddha said: pull the arrow out first, treat the wound first; those questions can wait.\nYou are the one with the arrow in you now. Who was wrong, why it happened to you — let those wait. Pull the arrow out first: see a doctor, keep the evidence, find one person you trust.\nOthers can help pursue the blame. No one can heal the wound but you.'
},

'幻听、觉得被监视、情绪忽高忽低':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。听到别人听不到的声音、总觉得被盯着，这不是你想太多，也不是意志力的事——请尽快去正规医院精神科看一次，让家人陪着你一起去。越早看越好治，这不丢人。见到医生之前，别一个人待着，也别用酒去压它。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Hearing voices others do not hear, or feeling watched all the time, is not overthinking and not a failure of willpower — please see a psychiatrist as soon as you can, and bring a family member with you. Earlier treatment usually works better, and there is no shame in it. Until you see the doctor, do not stay alone, and do not try to drown it with alcohol.',
  dharma:'有人夜里走山道，风把树影吹得乱晃，他以为前后都站着人。\n同行的老修行只说了一句：别看影子，看脚下这一块。\n他低头走了百来步，再看四周，除了树，什么都没有。\n老修行没说"你的影子是假的"，只说：路要一步一步走。\n你现在也一样——不必去跟那些声音争真假，先走脚下这一步：去看医生，让家人陪着，把觉睡稳。',
  dharmaEn:'A man walked a mountain path at night. The wind shook the shadows of the trees, and he was sure there were people standing all around him.\nThe old practitioner walking with him said only: do not look at the shadows. Look at this patch under your feet.\nHe walked a hundred steps looking down, then looked up — nothing there but trees.\nThe old man never said "your shadows are not real". He only said: the road is walked one step at a time.\nIt is the same for you — you do not have to argue with those voices about what is true. Take the step under your feet: see the doctor, let your family come with you, and get your sleep steady.'
  },

  '查出抑郁症、不敢跟人说':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。查出来那一刻，心里多半是又沉又怕——怕别人知道，也怕自己一直好不了。先说一句：病是病，不是你这个人不好，也不是谁在罚你。你不需要今天就告诉所有人，先告诉一个信得过的人，就够了。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. That moment of diagnosis is heavy and frightening — afraid others will know, and afraid you will never get better. One thing first: an illness is an illness. It is not a verdict on who you are. You do not have to tell everyone today. One person who can be trusted is enough.',
  dharma:'山里有个种药的人。\n有人问他：药为什么这么苦。他说：苦的才治病，甜的多半只哄嘴。\n又有人问他：那我什么时候能好。他说：你先按时喝，别总盯着碗看。\n你现在也一样——按医生说的治，把日子一天一天过。好不好不靠今天想通，靠今天做到。\n今晚只做一件：找一个人说一句"我最近不太好"。',
  dharmaEn:'There was a man in the mountains who grew medicinal herbs.\nSomeone asked him: why is medicine so bitter? He said: bitter medicine is what heals; sweet things mostly just please the mouth.\nSomeone else asked: then when will I get better? He said: take it on time first, and stop staring at the bowl.\nIt is the same for you — follow the treatment the doctor laid out, and let the days pass one at a time. Getting better comes from what you do today, not from understanding it today.\nTonight, do one thing only: tell one person, "I have not been well lately."'
  },

  '抑郁到不想动、起不来床':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下，别急着起来。你现在起不来，不是懒，也不是没出息，是病把你的力气拿走了。今天不要求你恢复什么，只求你做成一件小得不能再小的事——坐起来，喝口水。做成了，今天就没白过。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first — there is no hurry to get up. You cannot get up right now not because you are lazy or useless, but because the illness has taken your strength. Today asks nothing of you except one small thing: sit up, and drink some water. If you do that, the day was not wasted.',
  dharma:'冬天的高原，牛不出圈，人也不出门。\n有人问放牧的老人：这一冬怎么过。他说：不想远的事，只想今天这几步——添草、化冰、看看天。\n春天不是一下子来的，是这些"今天几步"堆出来的。\n你现在也一样。不求今天变好，只求今天动一下。\n今晚就做一件：坐起来，把脚放到地上，坐三分钟。',
  dharmaEn:'On the winter plateau, the cattle stay in the pen and people stay indoors.\nSomeone asked the old herder: how do you get through a winter like this? He said: I do not think about far-off things. I only think of today’s few steps — add hay, melt ice, look at the sky.\nSpring does not arrive all at once. It is piled up out of those few steps taken today.\nIt is the same for you. Do not ask to feel better today — ask only to move a little today.\nTonight, do one thing: sit up, put your feet on the floor, and sit there for three minutes.'
  },

  '吃抗抑郁药难受、怕依赖、想停药':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。吃药难受是真的难受，怕依赖、怕吃一辈子，也都是实在的担心，不是你想太多。但有一句要拦住你：别自己把药停了。想减、想停，都拿去跟开药的医生谈——他见过很多人这样走过，知道怎么让你少受罪。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. The side effects are real, and the fear of dependence or of taking medicine for life is a real fear — not you overthinking. But one thing should stop you: do not stop the medicine on your own. If you want to reduce it or stop it, take that to the doctor who prescribed it. They have walked many people through this and know how to make it easier.',
  dharma:'有人问师父：我每天要吃药，心里难受。\n师父说：那你先把药吃了，再说难受。\n他照做，吃了三个月。\n师父再问：还难受吗。他说：不怎么难受了，倒是能睡了。\n你这一段也一样——先把今天这顿吃了，别急着跟药算总账。\n今晚只做一件：按医生给的量把药吃了，然后在纸上写一句今天什么感觉，复诊时带去。',
  dharmaEn:'Someone asked his teacher: I have to take medicine every day and it troubles me.\nThe teacher said: take the medicine first, then tell me about the trouble.\nHe did that for three months.\nThe teacher asked again: still troubled? He said: not much — but I can sleep now.\nYour stretch is the same — take today’s dose first, and do not settle accounts with the medicine yet.\nTonight, do one thing: take the dose the doctor set, then write one line on paper about how you feel today and bring it to your next visit.'
  },

  '抑郁好了又犯、看不到头':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。好一阵又犯，是最磨人的，像白走了一段路。可这不是失败，也不是你不够努力——抑郁本来就有反复的脾气。上一次你走过去过，这一次也走得过去，只是要再走一遍，还得把医生说的疗程走完。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Getting better and then falling back is the most wearing thing — it feels like the earlier walk was wasted. But this is not failure, and not a sign you did not try hard enough. Depression has a relapsing nature. You made it through once before; you will make it through again. It just has to be walked again, this time finishing the course the doctor laid out.',
  dharma:'海边的潮水，一天涨落两次。\n有人问老渔人：浪来了怎么办。他说：浪来了就收网，退下去就补网。\n他从不指望海一直是平的。\n你犯病也是这样——来了就应对，退了就养着，不必因此骂自己半途而废。\n今晚只做一件：写下你上次犯病前最早出现的两个信号，贴在看得见的地方。',
  dharmaEn:'The tide by the sea rises and falls twice a day.\nSomeone asked an old fisherman: what do you do when the waves come? He said: when the waves come I haul in the nets; when the water retreats I mend them.\nHe never expected the sea to stay flat.\nYour relapses work the same way — deal with it when it comes, tend yourself when it goes. There is no need to call yourself a quitter.\nTonight, do one thing: write down the two earliest signals before your last episode, and put the note where you can see it.'
  },

  '家人朋友抑郁了、不知道怎么陪':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。你想帮他，这份心已经是一半的力气了。他不会因为你话说得不好就怪你，他缺的不是道理，是有人肯待在这儿。你只要做两件：陪他去一次医院，和他说话时不急着纠他。也别忘了，陪的人也会累，你歇一歇不算不管他。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. That wish to help is already half the strength. He will not blame you for saying the wrong thing; what he lacks is not advice but someone willing to stay nearby. You only have to do two things: go with him to one appointment, and do not rush to correct him when he talks. And one more thing — the one who accompanies also gets tired. Resting does not mean abandoning him.',
  dharma:'两个僧人走山路。一个跌了跤，走不动。\n另一个没背他，也没催他，只放慢脚步，一起坐在石头上，等他自己站起来。\n后来那人问：你当时为什么不说点道理。他说：我说了，他未必听得进；我坐着，他就知道还有人。\n你陪一个抑郁的人，能做的也是坐着。\n今晚只做一件：陪他吃一顿饭，饭桌上不提"你要振作"。',
  dharmaEn:'Two monks walked a mountain path. One fell and could not go on.\nThe other did not carry him and did not hurry him. He only slowed down, sat on a rock with him, and waited for him to stand up himself.\nLater the man asked: why did you not say something wise then? He said: if I had spoken, he might not have heard it. Sitting there, he knew someone was with him.\nThat is what you can do for a person with depression — sit there.\nTonight, do one thing: share a meal with him, and do not bring up "just cheer up" at the table.'
  },

  '微笑抑郁、看起来挺好、心里是空的':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。人前还能笑，是你这些年学会的本事，不是你虚伪。可笑得久了，连自己都忘了里面还压着一块。在这儿不用对谁笑，就坐一会儿。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Still being able to smile in front of others — that is a skill you learned over the years, not hypocrisy. But after smiling so long, even you forget what is still pressed down inside. Here you do not have to smile for anyone. Just sit a while.',
  dharma:'有个戏子，唱了一辈子笑角。\n散场后有人问他：你台上笑得那么好，台下怎么不笑。他说：台上那是我吃饭的本事，台下这张脸才是我。\n卸了妆，他才算回到家。\n你也是——笑是你的本事，不是你的全部。\n今晚只做一件：找个没人看的地方，把脸放松五分钟，想哭就哭。',
  dharmaEn:'There was a performer who played the comic role his whole life.\nAfter the show someone asked him: you laugh so well on stage, why do you not laugh off stage? He said: on stage that is how I make a living; this face off stage is who I am.\nOnly after taking off the makeup was he home.\nIt is the same for you — the smile is your skill, not the whole of you.\nTonight, do one thing: find a place where no one is watching, let your face rest for five minutes, and cry if you need to.'
  },

  '病耻感、要不要告诉单位、该不该请假':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。你不是怕丢脸，是怕丢了饭碗——这份担心是实在的，不是你多想。也不用对所有人坦白：该说的人说清楚，不该说的不必解释。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. What you fear is not losing face but losing your livelihood — and that fear is real, not overthinking. Nor do you owe everyone the truth: say what is needed to those who need it, and explain nothing to the rest.',
  dharma:'小沙弥的衣服破了一块，补了块补丁。\n他一整天拿手捂着那块布走路，谁看他他都躲。\n老和尚说：你不捂，还没人看；你一捂，满院子都盯着你那只手。\n该跟谁说起你的病、说多少，你自己定；但先别替所有人看不起你。\n今晚只做一件：写下三个"必须让知道的人"，其余的人，先放下。',
  dharmaEn:'A young monk’s robe tore, and he patched it.\nAll day he walked with his hand over the patch, shrinking from anyone who looked his way.\nThe old monk said: if you did not cover it, no one would notice; by covering it, the whole courtyard stares at your hand.\nWho to tell about your illness, and how much, is yours to decide — but do not look down on yourself on everyone else’s behalf.\nTonight, do one thing: write down the three people who truly need to know, and set the rest aside.'
  },

  '情绪低落多久算抑郁、要不要去看医生':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。你不是小题大做——会问"我到底算不算病"的人，多半已经难受一阵子了。不用急着给自己下判断，先看看是从什么时候开始的、哪儿不舒服；该不该看医生，交给医生来判。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. You are not making a fuss — anyone who asks "is this really an illness" has usually been struggling for a while. Do not rush to diagnose yourself. Just notice when it started, and what is not right — poor sleep, poor appetite, and the like; whether it needs a doctor is for a doctor to decide.',
  dharma:'有人问师父：我这心里发闷，算不算病。\n师父说：你先老实答我——吃饭香不香，睡得好不好，事还做不做得动。\n他答：都不太行，已经一个多月了。\n师父说：那你该去问大夫，别问我。\n今晚只做一件：把"什么时候开始的、哪儿不好"写在纸上，明天挂号时带上。',
  dharmaEn:'Someone asked his teacher: this heaviness in my chest — is it an illness?\nThe teacher said: answer me honestly first — does food taste of anything, do you sleep, can you still get things done?\nHe answered: none of them really, for over a month now.\nThe teacher said: then you should be asking a doctor, not me.\nTonight, do one thing: write down when it started and what is not right, and take the note with you when you book the appointment.'
  },

  '孩子说不想活、抑郁了、家长怎么办':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。听见孩子说那句话，你心里一定慌得厉害——这份怕是对的，它提醒你这件事不能等。先别急着讲道理，也别追问他为什么这样想。让他先知道一件事：无论如何，你不会放弃他。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. Hearing your child say that must have shaken you badly — and that fear is right, because it tells you this cannot wait. Do not rush into reasoning, and do not press him on why he feels that way. Let him know one thing first: whatever happens, you are not giving up on him.',
  dharma:'有个母亲抱着孩子过河，水急，孩子吓得直哭。\n她一句话没说，只把孩子抱得更紧，一步一步走。\n到了对岸，孩子才说：娘，刚才我以为我们要淹死了。\n她说：我知道，所以我才一直抱着你。\n今晚只做一件：坐到孩子旁边，说一句"我在这儿，你不用一个人扛"。',
  dharmaEn:'A mother carried her child across a river. The water was fast, and the child cried in fear.\nShe said nothing at all. She only held him tighter and kept walking, step by step.\nOnly on the far bank did the child say: Mother, I thought we were going to drown.\nShe said: I know. That is why I never let go of you.\nTonight, do one thing: sit down beside your child and say, "I am here. You do not have to carry this alone."'
  },

  '查不出病、浑身难受、是不是想出来的':{
  compassion:'朋友，先坐下。检查都说没事，人却难受得厉害——这种滋味比查出病还折磨人，因为没人信你。可难受是真的，不是你矫情，也不是你想出来的。今天先不必替自己下结论，把身体和心情两件事都说给医生听，就够开始了。',
  compassionEn:'Friend, sit down first. The tests say nothing is wrong, yet you feel terrible — and that is harder than having a diagnosis, because no one believes you. But the distress is real. You are not being dramatic, and you are not imagining it. You do not have to settle what it is today; telling a doctor about both your body and your mood is enough to begin.',
  dharma:'有人总觉得自己身上有病，跑了很多地方，都说没事。\n他去问师父。师父说：你觉得疼，那就是真疼。\n他问：那我该怎么办。师父说：该看医生就看医生，该说出来就把心里那口气说出来。\n身上的疼和心里的堵，本就是一回事。\n今晚只做一件：跟一个信得过的人说一句实话——"我身体查不出问题，但心里也不好受"。',
  dharmaEn:'A man was sure something in his body was wrong. He went from place to place, and everyone said nothing was found.\nHe asked his teacher. The teacher said: if you feel pain, then the pain is real.\nHe asked: so what should I do? The teacher said: see a doctor when a doctor is needed, and when it is time to speak, speak the thing your heart has been holding.\nThe ache in the body and the knot in the heart are one matter.\nTonight, do one thing: tell one person you trust the plain truth — "the tests found nothing, but I am not well inside either."'
  }
  };
